hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1801","624 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn al-As informed us, from Sa'id ibn Amr ibn al-As, that when Adi judged four hundred and eighty dirhams, Amr ibn Hurayth sent him thirty thousand; so he divided it that day before leaving among those present with him, wearing a cloak; when it reached Amr ibn Hurayth that he had divided it, he sent to her her trousseau and what sets her right; and she was called Usdah bint Adi."
"1802","625 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: It is written in some books: the dowry of the virgin is forty dirhams, and the dowry of the previously married woman is twenty dirhams, so that none may say: I find nothing to marry with, and then fornicate."
"1803","626 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, who said: Marriage upon whatever they mutually agree is dowry."
"1804","Chapter on secret marriage. 627 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus informed us, from Ubayd, saying: al-Hasan narrated to us that a man married a woman secretly and used to visit her; a neighbor of hers saw him and accused him concerning her, so he appealed against him to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him; Umar said to him: Your proof of marrying her. He said: O Commander of the Believers, our affair was private, but I had her family witness it. So Umar warded the hadd from his accuser and said: Guard the chastity of these women, announce this marriage, and he forbade mut'ah."
"1805","628 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that he heard him say: Secret marriage is unlawful."
"1806","629 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah and Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Muhammad ibn Hatib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The distinction between the lawful and the unlawful is the voice and the beating of the tambourine."
"1807","630 - Sa'id narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, saying: I heard Rabi'ah say: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, heard the sound of a kabar and said: What is this? It was said: A wedding. He said: Announce marriage."
"1808","631 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Hamzah ibn Suhayb, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: The tambourine was beaten and singing took place over Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf on the night of consummation."
"1809","632 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: I was told that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, when he heard a sound he disliked, asked about it; if it was said: A wedding or a circumcision, he approved it."
"1810","633 - Sa'id narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Salim al-Khayyat, from al-Hasan, that a man married secretly, and a man said to him: I see you entering upon so-and-so; you must be fornicating with her. That was raised to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him; he said: She is my wife; so Umar did not flog the accuser."
"1811","634 - Sa'id narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us; Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman said, from Ata, concerning a man who says to a man: You approach your wife only unlawfully: There is no hadd upon him."
"1812","635 - Sa'id narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Ilyas narrated to us, from Rabi'ah, the man of opinion, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Announce marriage, and beat upon it the sieve-drum."
"1813","Chapter on marrying a small girl. 636 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Sayyar narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, that a man on a journey said to his companions: Which of you will slaughter a sheep for us, and I shall marry him to the first daughter born to me? A man of the people did that and slaughtered a sheep for them; then a daughter was born to the man, so he came to him and said: My wife. They came to Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah have mercy on him, and Ibn Mas'ud said: The marriage is binding by the sheep, and she has the dowry of her peers, with neither loss nor excess."
"1814","637 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah, something like that."
"1815","638 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that some people on a journey, and a man of the people said: Who will slaughter a sheep for the people, and he shall have my daughter, or he said: a daughter to be born to me? A man of them slaughtered; when a daughter was born to him, that was mentioned to Abdullah, may Allah have mercy on him, and he said: You have taken possession of the woman, but this is not a dowry."
"1816","639 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, who said: al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam visited Qudamah ibn Maz'un to console him in illness, and al-Zubayr was given glad tidings of a girl while with him; Qudamah said to him: Marry her to me. Al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam said to him: What would you do with a small girl in this state? He said: Yes; if I live, she is the daughter of al-Zubayr, and if I die, she is the dearest of those who inherit me. So he married her to him."
"1817","640 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ibn Qusayt, who said: A man was given glad tidings of a girl, and a man said: Give her to me. He said: She is yours. Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib was asked about that and said: A gift is not lawful for anyone after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had he given her a dower, even a whip, she would have been lawful to him."
"1818","641 - Sa'id narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah have mercy on him, that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to offer myself to you. He looked at her, raising his gaze and lowering it, then bowed his head. A man of his Companions stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, if you have no need of her, marry her to me. He said: Do you have anything? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Go to your family and see whether you find anything. He went, then returned and said: No, by Allah, I found nothing. He said: Go, even an iron ring. He went, then returned and said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, not even an iron ring; but this is my lower garment. Sahl said: He had no cloak, so half of it would be hers. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What would you do with your lower garment? If you wear it, nothing of it will be upon her, and if she wears it, nothing of it will be upon you. The man sat until his sitting grew long. He said: What do you have of the Qur'an? He said: With me are such-and-such a surah and such-and-such a surah, naming them. He said: Do you recite them by heart? He said: Yes. He said: Go, I have given her to you in marriage for what you have of the Qur'an."
"1819","642 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: Abu Arfajah al-Fayishi narrated to us, from Abu al-Nu'man al-Azdi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married a woman for a surah of the Qur'an, then said: It shall not be a dowry for anyone after you."
"1820","643 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Umm al-Hakam sought from his wife, the daughter of Jarir, in his illness, something of her inheritance from him, but she refused him; so he married two other women over her, and Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan upheld that."
"1821","644 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, who said: I heard al-Sha'bi say concerning a man who marries a woman while ill: His marrying, his selling and his buying are valid."
"1822","645 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us; Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: We uphold his marrying in his illness."
"1823","646 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Nafi', that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rabi'ah married a cousin of his in Uthman's time - she being the one Umar had married and then divorced - in his illness so that she would inherit him; then he died and she inherited him."
"1824","Chapter on the prohibition of a man proposing over his brother's proposal. 647 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I heard him say: A man shall not propose over his brother's proposal until he marries or leaves off."
"1825","648 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us; Awf informed us, saying: al-Hasan informed us, saying: I was told that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man shall not propose over his brother's proposal, nor outbid over his brother's bargain."
"1826","649 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man married a woman over her maternal aunt, so Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, separated them."
"1827","Chapter on a man not marrying a woman over her paternal or maternal aunt. 650 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Abi Salamah informed us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a woman be married over her paternal aunt or over her maternal aunt."
"1828","651 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who heard Abu Salamah narrate from Abu Hurayrah, who said: He forbade that a woman be married over a daughter and over her maternal aunt. [Flag: wording garbled in source; editors note an omission.]"
"1829","652 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a woman be married over her paternal aunt or over her maternal aunt, and he forbade that a woman be married over her brother's daughter or her sister's daughter; he forbade that the elder be married over the younger, or the younger over the elder."
"1830","653 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us; Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman shall not be married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt, nor shall a woman ask for her sister's divorce to scoop up what is in her bowl and be married, for she shall have only what was written for her."
"1831","654 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A woman and her paternal aunt shall not be joined, nor she and her maternal aunt; nor shall a woman ask for her sister's divorce to empty what is in her bowl and marry, for she shall have only what was decreed for her."
"1832","Chapter on paternal cousins' daughters and combining them. 655 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, who said: The marriage of two paternal cousins' daughters was disliked, because of discord between them."
"1833","656 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in joining two paternal cousins' daughters, and two maternal cousins' daughters."
"1834","657 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, that a son of Ali joined two paternal cousins' daughters, the two paternal uncles not knowing of that; in the morning there were women not knowing to whom to go, to this one or to this one. Amr said: So I said to al-Hasan ibn Muhammad: What is this you have done? He said: It is dearer to us than them. [Flag: last phrase obscure in source.]"
"1835","Chapter on stipulations in marriage. 658 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr Marthad al-Yazani, who said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir narrate, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most deserving of stipulations you fulfill are those by which you made private parts lawful."
"1836","659 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far al-Ansari informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, who said: A man of al-Namr ibn Qasit narrated to me, saying: I heard Suhayb ibn Sinan say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any man who gives a woman a dowry while Allah knows he does not intend to pay it to her, deceiving her by Allah and making her private part lawful falsely, shall meet Allah on the day he meets Him as an adulterer; and any man who borrows a debt from a man while Allah knows he does not intend to repay him, deceiving him by Allah and making his wealth lawful falsely, shall meet Allah on the day he meets Him as a thief."
"1837","660 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who heard Jabir ibn Zayd say: When a man stipulates for the woman her house, it is for what he made lawful of her private part."
"1838","661 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Abi Dhubab narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Yasar, who said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib about a man who stipulates for a woman her house. He said: He takes her out wherever he wishes."
"1839","662 - Sa'id narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Ismail ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi al-Muhajir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, who said: I witnessed Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, brought a woman for whom her husband had assigned her house; Umar said: She has her stipulation. A man said: Then they will divorce us. Umar said: The endpoints of rights are at the stipulations."
"1840","663 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ismail ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, who said: I was sitting with Umar while my knee touched his knee, when a man said: O Commander of the Believers, I married this woman and stipulated for her her house, yet I gather for my affair that I shall move to such-and-such a land. He said: She has her stipulation. A man said: Men are ruined then; no woman will wish to divorce her husband but she will divorce. Umar said: Muslims are upon their stipulations at the endpoints of their rights."
"1841","664 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Karim al-Jazari narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah, that Mu'awiyah was brought such a case and consulted Amr ibn al-As, who said: She has her stipulation."
"1842","665 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Qays al-Masir, who said: I witnessed Shurayh when a man came to him and said: I am a man of Syria. He said: Welcome to the remnant. He said: I married a woman. He said: With harmony and sons. He said: I stipulated for her her house. He said: Muslims are at their stipulations. He said: Judge between us. He said: I have done so."
"1843","666 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: Adi ibn Artah came to Shurayh and said: I am a man of Syria. He said: Welcome and greetings. He said: I married a woman. He said: With harmony and sons. He said: I stipulated for her her house. He said: The stipulation owns. He said: I wished to return to my family. He said: You are more deserving of your family. He said: Then where are you? He said: Between you and the wall. He said: Then judge between us. He said: I have done so."
"1844","667 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abbad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, concerning a man who marries a woman and stipulates for her her house: Allah's stipulation is before hers."
"1845","668 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us; Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, who said: The marriage is valid but the stipulation is void."
"1846","669 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, the same as that."
"1847","670 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Farqad, from Sa'id ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, that a man married a woman in Umar ibn al-Khattab's time and stipulated for her that he would not take her out; so Umar ibn al-Khattab lifted the stipulation from him and said: The woman is with her husband."
"1848","671 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, that Ali and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, were asked about a man who marries a woman while she stipulates upon him that separation, intercourse and the dowry are in her hand. They said: You are blind to the sunnah and entrusted the affair to one unfit; upon you is the dowry, and in your hand are separation and intercourse."
"1849","672 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: Every stipulation in marriage, the marriage demolishes it except divorce; and every stipulation in a sale, the sale demolishes it except manumission."
"1850","673 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mutarrif informed us, from Ibrahim, that he said the same as that."
"1851","674 - Sa'id narrated to us; Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, who said: I was sitting with Shurayh when a woman came to him and said: O Abu Umayyah, this man came to me, not hoping to marry me, so I said to him: Will you marry me? He said: Are you mocking me? Then I married myself to him, gave him four thousand dirhams of what is mine, and traded for him in my wealth until his wealth grew within mine like the mark on a camel's side; now he claims he will divorce me and marry over me. Shurayh said to the man: What do you say? He said: She spoke the truth. Shurayh asked the notables around him, and they claimed that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought the like of what came to you, and he said: You are more entitled to divorce and marriage as between you and four women; if you divorce, divorce is in your hand, but return to her her wealth and the like of it from your wealth for what you made lawful of her private part. Shurayh said: This is what reached us from him; it is my judgment between you; stand."
"1852","675 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that he held a man's marrying a woman on condition he takes her on pilgrimage to be valid; if he divorces her before entering upon her, she has half of what one like her performs pilgrimage with."
"1853","676 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that he held marriage for a house and a servant to be valid."
"1854","677 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in a man marrying for a house and a servant."
"1855","678 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq informed me that a man married a woman and stipulated for her a house, giving her covenants and pledges; they disputed to Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, who asked al-Qasim and Salim ibn Abdullah, and they said: Allah's covenants must not be transgressed."
"1856","679 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayd al-Kala'i, from Makhul, concerning a man who proposes to a man for his daughter or sister, and he says: I shall not do it unless you divorce your wife; so he divorces her once, then marries this one, then wishes to take back the first. He said: That is his. He said: And how, if the one who married him said: I married you only upon separation from your wife, while the other said: I stipulated to you only that I divorce her, and I have divorced her, and I am taking her back? Makhul said: He may take her back if he wishes."
"1857","680 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayd, from Makhul, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said concerning a man who stipulates for a woman her house: He shall not take her out unless she wishes, for the endpoints of rights are the stipulations; and Makhul held that view."
"1858","Chapter on marrying daytime wives. 681 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in marrying daytime wives, while Ibn Sirin disliked that."
"1859","682 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who marries a woman and assigns her known days of the month: he saw no harm in it, while Ibn Sirin disliked that."
"1860","683 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan and Ata, that they saw no harm in marrying daytime wives."
"1861","684 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mutarrif informed us, from al-Hakam and Hammad, that they disliked that."
"1862","685 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: This is a corrupt stipulation."
"1863","Chapter on stipulations at the marriage contract. 686 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Awf informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that when he married off a daughter of his or of his freedwomen, he would say: Upon you is to hold with kindness or release with goodness."
"1864","687 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: When Ibn Umar married, he would say: I marry you upon what Allah, blessed and exalted, commanded: holding with kindness or releasing with goodness."
"1865","688 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from a man I thought was Sulayman, who said: I proposed to Ibn Umar for a freedwoman of his, and he said: I marry you upon what Allah commanded: holding with kindness or releasing with goodness."
"1866","689 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: One who heard Abu Bakr ibn Hafs narrate informed us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: I joined Ibn Umar and proposed to him for his daughter; he said to me: The son of Abu Abdullah is indeed worthy to be married; we praise our Lord and pray upon our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we have married you upon what Allah commanded: holding with kindness or releasing with goodness."
"1867","690 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that he disliked a man placing his hand upon a woman he had married until he names her dowry or advances something."
"1868","Chapter on seeking refuge from the unsalability of unmarried women and the like. 691 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Maryam, who said: Hakim ibn Umayr and Damrah ibn Habib narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from the unsalability of unmarried women, and would supplicate for them a ready market of marriage."
"1869","692 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Salim informed us, saying: Abdullah ibn Thabit al-Kindi informed us that a man proposed to a man for his sister and he married her to him; he sent her slaughter-camels, which she accepted and divided among her quarter; then she denied the marriage afterwards, so they disputed to Shurayh, who said to the man: Your proof that she consented? He said: I have no proof except that her brother married her to me, and he admits that, and the slaughter-camels I gifted her she accepted and divided among her quarter. Shurayh said: Had I judged for anyone without proof, I would have judged for you; then he made the woman swear by Allah, besides whom there is no god, that she had neither consented, nor permitted, nor approved; so she swore, and he made her liable for the price of the slaughter-camels."
"1870","Chapter on a woman married in her waiting period. 693 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Nu'aym, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that a man married a woman, and when he had her, he found her pregnant; so he raised that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who separated them, assigned her the dowry, and flogged her one hundred."
"1871","694 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, concerning one who married in her waiting period: Umar separated them and said: The marriage was unlawful and the dowry was unlawful, so he placed the dowry in the public treasury."
"1872","695 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that Umar was brought a woman who had married in her waiting period; so he separated them and punished her, placed the dowry in the public treasury as a punishment for her, and said: They shall never join."
"1873","696 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, separated them and struck them, saying: She shall never return to him, and he placed the dowry in the public treasury."
"1874","697 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, retracted his word concerning the dowry and assigned it to her for what he made lawful of her private part."
"1875","698 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Umar said to one who married in her waiting period: He separated them and said: They shall never marry; he assigned her the dower for what he made lawful of her private part, and ordered her to observe waiting from this one and waiting from this one."
"1876","699 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, separated them and assigned her the dowry for what he made lawful of her private part, saying: When her waiting period ends, if she wishes to marry him, she may do so. Hushaym said: And this is the view with us."
"1877","700 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, saying: Ibrahim said: They are separated, another marries her, then she completes what remains of her waiting from the first, then observes waiting from the other. Al-Sha'bi said: She observes waiting from this other one, then observes the remainder of her waiting from the first."
"1878","701 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi: There was between them, and one of them said: She observes waiting from the first, while the other said: She begins from the other. Ibrahim said: If you... [Flag: tail garbled in source.]"
"1879","702 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ibn Shubrumah narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Sha'bi, asked about a man who divorces his wife and she marries in her waiting period, which of the two waitings does she begin with? Al-Sha'bi said: She begins with the waiting of the more recent of the two in her contact."
"1880","703 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: One of the Kufans informed us that he said to Ibrahim, where he said: She begins with the waiting from the first: What if she is pregnant from the other? Ibrahim fell silent and did not answer him."
"1881","Chapter on a woman whose husband is absent and she marries after him. 704 - Sa'id narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: When two waiting periods enter into one waiting period, one of them suffices her."
"1882","705 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, concerning a man absent from his wife, so she marries, then the first comes: He said: She observes a single waiting period."
"1883","706 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Fudayl narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, who said: Two waiting periods."
"1884","707 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a woman told her husband had died, so she marries, then news comes that her first husband is alive; when it reached her first husband, he divorced her thrice. He said: His divorcing her is a choice; she withdraws from this other for three cycles, then marries whom she wishes; if she is pregnant, her delivery is her cycle, then after that she observes two menstruations."
"1885","708 - Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, concerning a man absent from his wife, so his wife marries, then her husband arrives: He said: She observes waiting from the other, then she is handed to the first."
"1886","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said about the woman who married during her waiting period: ""They are to be separated, and she shall complete what remains of her waiting period from the first husband, then observe a waiting period from the second."""
"1887","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, about a woman whose husband's death was announced to her, so she married another man after him, then he died and she inherited from him, and then her first husband arrived. He said: ""She shall be handed over to him (the first husband), and she shall return to the heirs of the deceased whatever she took from his inheritance."""
"1888","Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Walid ibn Abi Hashim: a woman whose husband died, then she remarried, then gave birth while with (her new) husband after four months, and the husband denied it, so the matter was raised to Umar ibn al-Khattab. He asked the woman, and she said: ""By Allah, there was no man between the two, but my husband's last contact with me was fifteen days before his death; then he died, and I used to see blood."" So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, asked some women from the days of ignorance, and they said: ""This does happen."" So he separated the two and assigned the child to the first (husband)."
"1889","Chapter on what is reported about a woman who marries her slave. Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, who said: A woman who had married her slave was brought to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: ""What led you to this?"" She said: ""He is my right-hand possession; has Allah not permitted right-hand possession?"" So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, ordered that she be beaten, and a woman who had married without witnesses was brought and he beat her, and he wrote to the people of the garrison towns forbidding them from that."
"1890","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Husayn informed us, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah: a woman who had married a slave of hers was brought to Umar ibn al-Khattab, so he beat them both and separated them. The woman said: ""Does Allah, Mighty and Majestic, not say in His Book: 'or what your right hands possess'?"" And he wrote to the people of the garrison towns: ""Any woman who marries her slave, or marries without witnesses or a guardian, flog her the prescribed punishment."""
"1891","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan: a woman who had married her slave was brought to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, so he punished her, separated her from her slave, and forbade (future) husbands to her as a punishment for her."
"1892","Chapter on marrying a Jewish or Christian woman. Sa'id narrated: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Maryam al-Ghassani narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abi Talha, from Ka'b ibn Malik: he wanted to marry a Jewish or a Christian woman, so he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he forbade him, saying: ""She will not make you chaste."""
"1893","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from al-Salt ibn Bahram, who heard Abu Wa'il Shaqiq ibn Salama say: Hudhayfa married a Jewish woman, so Umar wrote to him: ""Divorce her."" He wrote back to him: ""Why? Is she unlawful?"" So he wrote to him: ""No, but I feared that you would take up the immoral women among them."""
"1894","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mughira informed us, al-Sha'bi narrated to us, who said: ""One of the six members of the consultative council married a Jewish woman."" I said to him: ""Was it al-Zubayr?"" Al-Sha'bi said: ""He was indeed of noble marriages."""
"1895","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Ibn Awn informed us, from Ibn Sirin: Hudhayfa married a Jewish woman, and Umar spoke to him about that. He said: ""Is she unlawful?"" He said: ""No, but you are a leader of the Muslims, so part from her."""
"1896","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan: he saw no harm in marrying a Jewish or Christian woman alongside a Muslim wife. He said: ""And the division (of nights) between them is equal."""
"1897","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mutarrif informed us, from al-Sha'bi and Ubayda, from Ibrahim: they both said: ""If he marries a Jewish or Christian woman alongside a Muslim woman, the division between them is equal, but if he accuses her (of adultery), he does not perform li'an (mutual imprecation) with her."""
"1898","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mansur and Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: ""Between every two spouses there is li'an (mutual imprecation)."""
"1899","Chapter on marrying a slave woman alongside a free woman, and a free woman alongside a slave woman. Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, who said: I heard Ibn al-Musayyib say: ""A free woman may be married alongside a slave woman, but a slave woman may not be married alongside a free woman; and one-third shall be allotted to the slave woman and two-thirds to the free woman."""
"1900","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, who said: ""A free woman may be married alongside a slave woman, but a slave woman may not be married alongside a free woman; and when he marries a free woman alongside her, one-third shall be allotted to the slave woman and two-thirds to the free woman."""
"1901","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: ""A free woman may be married alongside a slave woman, but a slave woman may not be married alongside a free woman unless she (the free woman) herself wishes that."""
"1902","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zirr and Abbad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: he used to say: ""When he marries a free woman alongside a slave woman and divides between them: one-third for the slave woman and two-thirds for the free woman."""
"1903","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan: he used to dislike marrying slave women in his time, saying: ""They were only permitted when one cannot afford a free woman."""
"1904","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan: he used to say the same."
"1905","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Abu Bishr informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, about His saying, Mighty and Majestic: ""And whoever among you cannot afford (tawlan)"": he said: ""Tawl means wealth; when he does not find the means to marry a free woman, he marries a slave woman."""
"1906","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim: he used to say: ""When he marries a free woman alongside a slave woman, it is dearer to me that he part from the slave woman, unless he fears al-anat (falling into sin); if he fears al-anat, he keeps her, allotting her one-third and two-thirds to the free woman, of himself and his wealth."""
"1907","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Ubayda narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: He said to me: ""Do you know what al-anat is?"" I said: ""What is that?"" He said: ""Fornication."""
"1908","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, and Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak: they both said: ""Al-anat is fornication."""
"1909","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Abu Bishr informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: ""One who marries a slave woman has barely escaped fornication. 'And that you be patient is better for you' — he said: (that is,) refraining from marrying slave women."""
"1910","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym informed us, Ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, who said: ""When he marries a free woman alongside a slave woman, that is the divorce of the slave woman. He is like one allowed carrion: he eats of it as much as he is compelled to, and when he can do without it, he refrains."""
"1911","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, about marrying a free woman alongside a slave woman. He said: ""She is like carrion, resorted to out of necessity; when Allah enriches you so you can do without her, then do without her."""
"1912","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mutarrif informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq: he used to say: ""When he marries a free woman alongside a slave woman, that is the divorce of the slave woman, and the two do not combine except for a slave (husband)."""
"1913","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq: he used to say about a slave: ""When he has a free wife, he may marry a slave woman alongside her if he wishes."""
"1914","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mughira and Sayyar informed us, from al-Sha'bi: he used to say: ""When he finds the means for a free woman, the slave woman becomes unlawful to him."""
"1915","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abbad, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: ""When he marries a free woman alongside a slave woman, the free woman gets two-thirds and the slave woman one-third."""
"1916","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Any free man who marries a slave woman has enslaved half of himself, and any slave who marries a free woman has freed half of himself."""
"1917","Sa'id narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Umar, the same."
"1918","Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated, one who heard al-Hasan narrated to me, saying: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a slave woman be married alongside a free woman."" [Flag: the narrator from al-Hasan is unnamed in the source.]"
"1919","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Amr, that Ibn Abbas said: ""Marrying a free woman alongside a slave woman is her (the slave woman's) divorce."""
"1920","Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, my father informed me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, who said: ""It is part of the Sunna that when a man marries a slave woman alongside a free wife, she (the free wife) has the choice: if she wishes, she leaves him, and if she wishes, she stays; and if she stays despite the harm, she gets two days and the slave woman one day."""
"1921","Chapter on a man who marries a woman and consummates with her before stipulating anything. Sa'id narrated: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated, from Mansur, from Talha ibn Musarrif, from Khaythama — Jarir said: I think it is from A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her — who said: ""A Muslim man who had nothing married a woman, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that his wife enter upon him, and enjoined good treatment of them; then the man prospered afterwards until he became among the notables."""
"1922","Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Talha ibn Musarrif, from Khaythama: a man of the Ansar married, and they said: ""O Messenger of Allah, he is poor and has nothing; shall we let her enter upon him when he has given her nothing of her dower?"" He said: ""Yes, let her enter upon him."""
"1923","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Abu Hamza Imran ibn Abi Ata informed us, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say — when a man asked him, saying that he had married a woman but was unable to pay her dower — he said: ""If you find nothing but one of your two sandals, give it to her and consummate with her."""
"1924","Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', from his father: So-and-so son of Hurmuz married Layla bint al-Ajma' in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, for four thousand, then consummated with her before giving her anything of her dower."
"1925","Sa'id narrated: Abu Awana narrated, from Imran ibn Abi Ata, from Ibn Abbas: he used to dislike that a man consummate with his wife until he gives her something."
"1926","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Hajjaj informed us, from Abu Ishaq: Kurayb ibn Abi Muslim — who was among the companions of Abd Allah — married a woman for four thousand, then consummated with her before giving her anything."
"1927","Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Kurayb ibn Hisham — who was among the companions of Abd Allah — that he married a woman for four thousand, then consummated with her before giving her anything of her dower. [Flag: source prints ""Kurayb ibn Hisham""; an edition note suggests the correct name may be Kurayb al-Hashimi — translated as printed.]"
"1928","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim: they both saw no harm in a man consummating with his wife before giving her anything."
"1929","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: ""When a woman of the people of Medina married, she would send to her husband: 'Spend the night with us so that I become entitled to the dower' — and that was before he gave her anything."""
"1930","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, from one who heard Qatada narrate from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: he saw no harm in consummating with her before giving her anything."
"1931","Sa'id narrated: Jarir narrated, from Mughira, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, about a man who marries a woman. He said: It used to be said: ""The best amity is that he not approach her until he brings her to his house."""
"1932","Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, who said: ""He saw no harm, once a man holds the marriage tie, in his consummating with her before paying her anything."""
"1933","Sa'id narrated: Attab ibn Bashir narrated, Khusayf informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: ""A man shall not enter upon his wife until he presents her something — a shirt, a cloak or veil, even a ring."""
"1934","Chapter on what makes the dower obligatory. Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""When the curtains are let down, the dower and the waiting period become obligatory."""
"1935","Sa'id narrated: Abu Awana narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Umar: he said: ""When the door is closed, the curtain let down, or the veil removed, the dower has become obligatory."""
"1936","Sa'id narrated: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""When the door is closed, the curtain let down, and the veil put aside, the dower becomes obligatory."""
"1937","Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, who said: Umar said: ""When the door is closed and the curtain let down, the dower has become obligatory."""
"1938","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zirr and Abbad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: he said: ""Whoever closes a door and lets down a curtain, the dower and the waiting period have become obligatory."""
"1939","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Awf informed us, from Zurara ibn Awfa, who said: ""The rightly-guided caliphs ruled that whoever closes a door and lets down a curtain, the dower and the waiting period have become obligatory."""
"1940","Sa'id narrated: Abu Awana narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, who said: ""When a man sees of his wife what none but he may lawfully see, the dower and the waiting period have become obligatory."""
"1941","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ali ibn Husayn, who said: He said to me: ""Was the curtain let down upon you and the door closed upon you?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""The dower has become obligatory upon you."""
"1942","Sa'id narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from his father, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, about a man who is alone with a woman: he says ""I did not touch her,"" and she says ""He did touch me"" — her word is accepted."
"1943","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mughira informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, about a man whose wife was brought in to him and he claimed he had not touched her. Shurayh said: ""I have not heard Allah, Mighty and Majestic, mention in the Qur'an any door or curtain. She gets half the dower, and the waiting period is upon her."""
"1944","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi: Amr ibn Nafi' divorced his wife though she had been brought in to him; he claimed he had not approached her while she claimed he had. She disputed with him before Shurayh, so he made Amr swear a solemn oath by Allah besides whom there is no god that he had not approached her, and ruled half the dower against him."
"1945","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Sayyar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, the same."
"1946","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Amr ibn Nafi' married the daughter of Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, then divorced her, claiming he had not approached her. They disputed with him before Shurayh, so he had him swear the oath and ruled half the dower against him."
"1947","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Azra, from Shurayh: he said to her (the wife): ""No, I do not believe you for your own benefit, and I suspect you for your own benefit."" Hushaym says: So the waiting period is upon you, and do not marry until you have completed the waiting period."
"1948","Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim: a man married a woman and used to spend the night with her, then divorced her; she said: ""He never approached me,"" though he used to spend the night with me while I was in my clothes. He said: ""The waiting period is upon her and she gets the (full) dower. Do you not see that if she claimed pregnancy she would be believed?"" [Flag: an edition collation note discusses the word ""claimed"" — translated as printed.]"
"1949","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Layth informed us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas: he used to say about a man whose wife is brought in to him and then he divorces her, claiming he did not touch her: ""Half the dower is upon him."""
"1950","Chapter on a man marrying off his son while he is small. Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: ""When a man marries off his son while he is small, the dower is upon the son, unless the father guarantees it."" Hushaym said: ""And that is the adopted opinion."""
"1951","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mujalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: ""It is upon the father."""
"1952","Sa'id narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father: he married his brother's son to his brother's daughter while both were small."
"1953","Chapter on staying with a virgin and a previously-married woman. Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, who said: When Umm Salama entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""You are not humbled before your family. If you wish, I shall stay seven (nights) with you, and otherwise I stay three with you, then I make the round."""
"1954","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: ""When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took Safiyya bint Huyayy, he stayed with her three (nights)."""
"1955","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilaba, from Anas, who said: ""When he marries a virgin while already having a previously-married wife, he stays with her seven (nights), then divides; and when he marries a previously-married woman, he stays with her three."" Khalid said in his narration: ""Had I said to him that he raised it (to the Prophet), I would have spoken the truth, but he said: 'The Sunna is likewise.'"""
"1956","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Humayd informed us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say the same."
"1957","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Humayd and Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: ""When he marries a virgin while already having a previously-married wife, he stays with her three (nights), and when he marries a previously-married woman, he stays with her two nights."""
"1958","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Khalid informed us, from Ibn Sirin: he said the same as al-Hasan."
"1959","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Shu'ba informed us, from al-Hakam: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umm Salama when she entered upon him: ""If you wish, I shall stay seven, and seven for my (other) wives."""
"1960","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from a man he named, the same."
"1961","Chapter on a man who marries a slave woman, a Jewish or Christian woman, then commits adultery. Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, and Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, and Yunus, from al-Hasan, and Hajjaj and Abd al-Malik, from Ata: they said about a free man who marries a slave woman then commits an indecency: he is flogged, not stoned."
"1962","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Hajjaj informed us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather: ""A slave woman does not confer ihsan (marital chastity) upon a free man, a free woman does not confer it upon a slave, and a Jewish or Christian woman does not confer it upon a Muslim; and if he accuses one of them, there is no li'an between her and her husband."""
"1963","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, Ayyub informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: Umar said from the pulpit: ""Do you know how many (wives) a slave may marry?"" A man stood up to him and said: ""I do."" He said: ""How many?"" He said: ""Two."""
"1964","Chapter on a slave marrying without his master's permission. Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, who said: ""A slave marries four."""
"1965","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, who said: ""A slave marries two."""
"1966","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: a slave boy of his married without his command, so he flogged them both the prescribed punishment, took everything he had given her, and separated them."
"1967","Sa'id narrated: Jarir narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, who said: ""When a slave marries with his master's permission, divorce is in the slave's hand; but when he marries without his master's permission and then his master learns of it and rejects his marriage, he is separated from his wife, his master takes whatever of her dower he finds intact, what she has consumed is hers, and if anyone deceived the woman, he owes her a dower like hers."""
"1968","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughira, from Ibrahim, and Husayn, from al-Sha'bi: they said: ""When he marries without his master's permission, the matter is up to the master: if he wishes he may ratify, and if he wishes he may reject; but when he marries with his permission, divorce is in the slave's hand."""
"1969","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan: he used to say: ""When the master separates the two, she keeps what she took for what he made lawful of her."""
"1970","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, who said: ""When the master separates the two, whatever of his slave boy's property he finds intact with her is his, and what she has consumed — nothing is due upon her."""
"1971","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Ubayda informed us, from Ibrahim: he used to say: ""What she has consumed is a debt upon her."" Hushaym said: ""And that is the adopted opinion."""
"1972","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Ibn Abi Layla and al-Hajjaj informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar; and Hajjaj, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh; and Mughira, from Ibrahim; and Yunus, from al-Hasan; and Husayn and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi: they said: ""When he marries with his master's command, divorce is in his hand; and when he marries without his command, the matter is up to the master: if he wishes he joins, and if he wishes he separates."""
"1973","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Khalid informed us, from Ibn Sirin: a slave boy married without his master's permission, and the matter was raised to al-Ash'ari, so he wrote to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him — and he had given her five she-camels as dower — so Umar wrote to him: ""Give her three and take two from her,"" or ""give her two and take three from her."" [Flag: source wording is ambiguous between the two phrasings — translated literally as printed.]"
"1974","Sa'id narrated: Abu Awana narrated, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Shurayh, who said: ""A slave's divorce is valid, but his marriage is not valid (without permission)."""
"1975","Sa'id narrated: Abu Awana narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: ""When a man marries his slave girl to his slave, divorce is in the slave's hand."""
"1976","Sa'id narrated: Abu Awana narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Mujahid, who said: ""He may take her away from him if he wishes, without divorce."""
"1977","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mansur informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: he used to say: ""The matter is up to the master, whether he permitted him or not."" And he would recite this verse: ""Allah sets forth the example of a slave who is owned and unable to do a thing."""
"1978","Sa'id narrated: Jarir narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: ""They used to compel a slave to marry, bringing him together with his previously-married wife, then closing the door upon them both."""
"1979","Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, about a slave who marries without his masters' permission. He said: ""Divorce is in the master's hand: if he wishes he ratifies, and if he wishes he rejects; and whatever of his property the master finds intact is his."""
"1980","Sa'id narrated: Khalid narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, about a slave who marries with his masters' permission. He said: ""Divorce is in the slave's hand."""
"1981","Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Mughira, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, about a man who marries a woman without naming a dower for her: he sent her something and she accepted it, then he consummated with her, then she demanded her dower. He said: ""That is not hers if he consummated with her and she was content."""
"1982","Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, who said: ""When the master permits marriage, divorce is in the slave's hand."""
"1983","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Ma'bad: a slave boy of Ibn Abbas divorced his wife twice, and Ibn Abbas said to him: ""Take her back."" He refused, so he said: ""She is yours; make her lawful to yourself by right-hand possession."""
"1984","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: a slave has no divorce except with his master's permission. He said: And he mentioned: ""Allah sets forth the example of a slave who is owned and unable to do a thing."""
"1985","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, al-Shaybani informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: ""The people of the Hijaz — or some of them — do not deem a slave's marriage or divorce valid except with his master's permission."""
"1986","Sa'id narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, who said: I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr about a man who permits his slave to marry: in whose hand is divorce? He said: ""In the hand of the one who married."" I said to him: ""But Jabir ibn Zayd says it is in the master's hand?"" He said: ""Jabir has erred."""
"1987","Chapter on a man marrying his like among women, meaning his peer. Sa'id narrated: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Abu al-Mujashi' al-Azdi, who said: A young woman whom they had married to a very old man was brought to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, for she had killed him. He said: ""O people, fear Allah; let a man marry his peer among women, and let a woman marry her peer among men — meaning one like her."""
"1988","Sa'id narrated: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Do not force your young women upon an ugly man, for they love what you love."""
"1989","Sa'id narrated: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam al-Ghassani narrated to us, from Habib ibn Ubayd: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like marriage in Ramadan, hoping for blessing in it. [Flag: chain is mursal — Habib ibn Ubayd does not name the Companion he heard it from.]"
"1990","Chapter on a man marrying an immoral woman. Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, about a man who marries a woman though she has committed adultery. He said: ""If he is not ashamed for his child to be taunted with that, let him marry her if he wishes."""
"1991","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, the same."
"1992","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, from al-Hasan: he used to say: ""Neither an open fornicatress nor one who takes a secret lover is lawful for a Muslim."""
"1993","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mansur and Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan: he used to say: ""He shall part from her if she does that, while she is with him, and shall not keep her."""
"1994","Sa'id narrated: ... Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, who said: ""If a man found ten men with his wife, she would not become unlawful to him."" [Flag: the source text has an ellipsis (""..."") before Abu Shihab, indicating a gap in the chain as printed.]"
"1995","Chapter on one who marries a leprous or insane woman. Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated to us: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Any man who marries a woman, consummates with her, then finds in her leprosy, insanity, or lepromatous disease — she gets the dower for his touching her, and it is due from whoever deceived him about her."""
"1996","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: Umar ibn al-Khattab ruled: ""Any woman married while having something of this ailment, without him knowing until he touched her — she gets her dower for what he made lawful of her private part, and her guardian shall compensate her husband the like of her dower."""
"1997","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: ""Any man who marries a woman and finds her insane, leprous, or affected with vitiligo — she is his wife; if he wishes he divorces, and if he wishes he keeps."""
"1998","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Any woman married while having vitiligo, insanity, leprosy, or a vaginal obstruction — her husband has the choice so long as he has not touched her: if he wishes he keeps, and if he wishes he divorces; but if he touched her, she gets the dower for what he made lawful of her private part."""
"1999","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi: he said: ""That is when he has consummated with her; but if he learns of that before consummating with her, then if he wishes he keeps, and if he wishes he parts without divorce."""
"2000","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim: he used to say: ""She is his wife; if he wishes he keeps, and if he wishes he divorces — whether he consummated with her or not. Free women are not like slave women: a free woman is not returned on account of an ailment."""
"2001","Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim: he said that."
"2002","Sa'id narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: ""Four are not permissible in a sale or a marriage: an insane woman, a leprous woman, a vitiliginous woman, and one with a vaginal deformity."""
"2003","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Khalid al-Hadhdha' informed us, who said: Adi ibn Artat wrote to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz about that, and Umar wrote back to him: ""He has entrusted his in-laws with what is greater than that; if he wishes he divorces, and if he wishes he keeps."""
"2004","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan: he used to say: ""If the guardian knew of that, the dower is upon him as he deceived him about her; and if he did not know, she is his wife: if he wishes he divorces, and if he wishes he keeps."""
"2005","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: ""Four are not permissible in a sale or a marriage unless he touches: if he touches, then it has become binding — insanity, leprosy, vitiligo, and vaginal obstruction."""
"2006","Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, Jamil ibn Zayd al-Ta'i narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Ka'b ibn Ujra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married a woman of Banu Ghifar; when she entered upon him and put off her clothes, he saw whiteness on her side, so he said: ""Put on your clothes and join your family."""
"2007","Sa'id narrated: Sharik narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, who said: ""A free woman is not returned on account of a defect."""
"2008","Sa'id narrated: Abu Mu'awiya narrated, a man narrated to us, from Jamil ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Ka'b ibn Ujra: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same as the preceding narration — ""he ordered a dower for her."" [Flag: one narrator in the chain is unnamed (""a man"") in the source.]"
"2009","Muhammad narrated to me: Abu Amr Sahl ibn Zanjala al-Razi narrated to me: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, who said: I asked al-Zuhri: ""Which of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was it who sought refuge from him?"" He said: Urwa narrated to me, from A'isha: when the daughter of al-Jawn al-Kilabiyya entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he went to draw near her, she said: ""I seek refuge with Allah."" So he said: ""You have sought refuge with the Mighty; gather your clothes and join your family."""
"2010","Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, from Ata, about a man who marries a woman and then, after consummating with her, an ailment appears in the man — vitiligo or leprosy. Ata said: ""His wife shall not be taken away from him."""
"2011","Chapter on marriage for prompt and deferred (dower). Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, about a man who marries for a prompt and a deferred (sum): ""It is all due immediately, unless it has a known term."""
"2012","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Ash'ath informed us, from al-Sha'bi: he used to say about the deferred part of the dower: ""Until there is divorce or death."""
"2013","Chapter on a man who marries a slave woman owned by two men, then buys the share of one of them. Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, about a man who marries a slave woman owned by two men, then buys the share of one of them. He said: ""Let him not approach her until the share of the other is secured."""
"2014","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated: it was narrated to me from Ibrahim: he said that."
"2015","Chapter on a man who marries a woman unlawful to him by kinship. Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, about a man who marries a woman who is his mahram (unmarriageable kin). He said: ""If he consummated with her, she gets the dower; and if he had not consummated with her, she gets no dower, and they shall be separated."" And Hammad said: ""She keeps what she took."""
"2016","Sa'id narrated: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, who said: ""If he had not consummated with her, the dower is void; but if he consummated with her, she gets what he named for her."""
"2017","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: ""If he had not consummated with her, she gets nothing; but if he had consummated with her, she keeps what she took."""
"2018","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Ash'ath informed us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: ""She gets nothing, whether he consummated with her or not. Would a man give a dower to his sister or his mother?"""
"2019","Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayd, from Makhul, about a man who marries a woman and finds her to be his milk-sister, without knowing. He said: ""If he had not consummated with her, there is no marriage between them and he takes back his property; but if he had consummated with her and seen of her what a man sees of his wife, though without touching her, her full dower becomes due; and if he divorced her before touching her and gave her half the dower, not knowing she was his sister, then learns afterwards — I deem that she return to him what she took from him, though I have heard nothing on it; her waiting period is that of a divorcee if he consummated with her, and if one of them dies, there is no inheritance between them."""
"2020","Sa'id narrated: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Sa'id ibn Yusuf al-Rahabi, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about a man who marries a woman, gives her her dower, and she turns out to be his milk-sister, without him having consummated with her. He said: ""She shall return to him the property he gave her, and they shall part."""
"2021","Chapter on mut'a (temporary marriage). Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Mecca for his umra, the women of the people of Medina adorned themselves, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained to him. He said: ""Enjoy mut'a with them, setting the term between you and them as three (days); I do not think a man will be alone with a woman for three (days) except that he turns his back on her (leaves her)."""
"2022","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: ""Mut'a with women was only for three days; there was none before that nor after it."""
"2023","Sa'id narrated: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated, I heard Amr ibn al-Harith narrate, from al-Rabi' ibn Sabra al-Juhani, from his father, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted us mut'a in the year of the Conquest. I set out, I and a man, to a young woman like a tall young camel, to contract mut'a; we sat before her, I wearing a cloak and he wearing a cloak, and we spoke to her, offering our two cloaks as her dower. I was younger than him, while his cloak was finer than mine; she kept looking at his cloak one time and at mine another, then she accepted me, so I married her and stayed with her three (days). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it, so I parted from her"" — or words to that effect."
"2024","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from al-Zuhri, from al-Rabi' ibn Sabra al-Juhani, from his father: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mut'a marriage in the year of the Conquest."
"2025","Sa'id narrated: Sufyan narrated, from al-Zuhri, who heard Abd Allah and al-Hasan, the two sons of Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hanafiyya, narrate from their father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: he said to Ibn Abbas: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mut'a marriage and the meat of domestic donkeys at the time of Khaybar."""
"2026","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah and al-Hasan, the two sons of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya, from their father: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by Ibn Abbas while he was giving fatwa that there is no harm in women's mut'a, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it, and the meat of domestic donkeys, on the day of Khaybar."""
"2027","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: ""They used to contract mut'a with women until Umar forbade it."""
"2028","Sa'id narrated: Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us: Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Nu'aym al-A'raj, who said: A man asked Abd Allah ibn Umar about women's mut'a, and he became angry, saying: ""We were not fornicators or open adulterers in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" Then he said: ""By Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Before the Hour there shall be the False Messiah (al-Dajjal), and thirty liars or more.'"""
"2029","Sa'id narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: ""There were two mut'as in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I forbid them both and punish for them."" [Flag: the report as printed ends without completing the enumeration; cf. 2030.]"
"2030","Sa'id narrated: Hushaym narrated, Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilaba, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""There were two mut'as in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I forbid them both and punish for them: the mut'a of women, and the mut'a of Hajj."""
"2031","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that 'Umar prohibited mut'ah with women and mut'ah of Hajj."
"2032","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, that 'Urwah used to forbid mut'ah marriage and say: It is outright zina."
"2033","Chapter on what has come concerning a man who commits zina though he married a woman but did not consummate with her. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Hanash ibn al-Mu'tamir, he said: A man who had confessed to zina against himself was brought to 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said to him: Are you muhsan? He said: Yes. He said: Then you are to be stoned. So he sent him up to prison, and in the evening he called for him and laid his case before the people, when a man said to him: He married a woman but did not consummate with her. 'Ali was glad at that, so he inflicted the hadd on him, separated him from his wife, and gave her half the dower, in the view of Simak."
"2034","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Hanash, he said: A man came to 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: I have committed zina. He said: You are then to be stoned if you are muhsan. He said: I owned - or married - a woman but did not consummate with her. He said: So he flogged him one hundred, separated the two, and gave her a portion of her dower."
"2035","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: If she commits zina before consummation with her, the hadd is inflicted, the two are separated, and she has no dower."
"2036","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say that."
"2037","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, concerning a woman who commits zina before consummation, he said: The two are separated, and she has no dower."
"2038","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: If he commits zina before consummating with her, the hadd is carried out on him, the two are separated, and she has no dower."
"2039","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, concerning His saying, mighty and majestic: {The fornicator does not marry except a fornicatress or a polytheist woman}, he said: {And marry the unmarried among you} abrogated it, so she is among the unmarried women of the Muslims."
"2040","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, the like of it."
"2041","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Whichever of the two commits zina is flogged with the hadd, while they remain upon their marriage. Hushaym said: And it is the correct view."
"2042","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi 'Amrah, from Sa'id, concerning His saying, mighty and majestic: {The fornicator does not marry except a fornicatress or a polytheist woman}, he said: It is not marriage, but rather intercourse."
"2043","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, al-Shaybani informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that a slave girl committed immorality and the hadd was carried out on her, then they came emigrating, and the girl repented, her repentance and conduct became good, and she was being sought in marriage from her uncle, but he disliked marrying her off until he disclosed what had happened with her, while he disliked publicizing that against her, so she mentioned that matter of hers to 'Umar, and he said: Marry them off as you marry off your righteous women."
"2044","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: A woman in Syria did something shameful, so he wrote to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: Marry her off and do not mention her misdeed. He said: Marry them off and do not mention their misdeed."
"2045","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who married a virgin slave girl and she committed immorality before consummation, he said: The two are separated, and she has no dower."
"2046","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, he said: She is flogged and remains with him, just as if he had committed immorality his wife would not be taken away from him."
"2047","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from al-Sha'bi, he said: If the virgin woman commits zina and is exiled, she remains with her husband upon her marriage, and if the virgin man does so, it is likewise."
"2048","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym informed us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: Women do not conclude the marriage tie."
"2049","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, the like of it."
"2050","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that the Sunnah with them is that a woman does not conclude the marriage tie for herself nor for another."
"2051","Chapter on what has come concerning the testimony of women in marriage. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about a man who married with the testimony of a man and a woman, he said: They should call another man to witness."
"2052","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from 'Ata', from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, that he allowed the testimony of women along with a man in marriage."
"2053","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid and Mutarrif informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he used to allow the testimony of women along with a man in marriage and divorce."
"2054","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used not to allow the testimony of women for divorce nor for the hudud."
"2055","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that he used not to allow the testimony of women for the hudud, and divorce is among the gravest of hudud."
"2056","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used not to allow the testimony of women for divorce."
"2057","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib informed us, he said: I asked Ibrahim about the testimony of a man and two women for divorce, and Ibrahim said: Even if Tamim ibn Salamah and such-and-such women testified to a divorce, that would not be valid."
"2058","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: The testimony of women is not valid for the hudud."
"2059","Chapter on a woman owning something of her husband. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: If a woman comes to own something of her husband, she becomes unlawful to him, but if she frees him the moment she owns him, they remain upon their marriage."
"2060","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: If a woman comes to own something of her husband, she has become unlawful to him and she is divorced with an irrevocable divorce, and if she frees him it is likewise."
"2061","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from al-Sha'bi and 'Ata', they said: She has become unlawful; if she is still of his concern, let him propose to her."
"2062","Chapter on a man who commits immorality with a woman then marries her. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, from his father, that a man married a woman, and she had a daughter while he had a son from another, and he committed immorality with her, then 'Umar came to Mecca, so they were both brought before him and he inflicted the hadd on them, and he was keen to bring the two together, but the boy refused that."
"2063","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me, he said: I asked Ibn 'Abbas about a man who committed immorality with a woman, may he marry her? He said: Yes, that is when he attains what is lawful."
"2064","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, he said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas, and I asked him about a man who committed zina with a woman, may he marry her? He said: That is when he sets her affair right."
"2065","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, that he asked Ibn 'Abbas, and Ibn 'Abbas said: The first is fornication and the latter is marriage."
"2066","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Abu Hashim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he was asked about that, and he said: Its beginning is fornication and its end is marriage."
"2067","Sa'id narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, the like of it."
"2068","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, the like of it."
"2069","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Ibn 'Abbas, and 'Abd al-Malik from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, and Dawud ibn Abi Hind from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he used to say: Its beginning is fornication and its end is marriage."
"2070","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Na'amah al-Dabbi informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he said: Its beginning is fornication and its end is marriage; she became lawful to him through his wealth."
"2071","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar informed us, from 'Ikrimah, that he used to say concerning a man who commits immorality with a woman then marries her, he said: His likeness is that of a man who took fruit of a palm tree without its owner's permission so it was unlawful, then he bought it so it became lawful to him."
"2072","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydah informed us, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Ali, that he was asked about that, he said: His likeness is only that of a man who came to a threshing floor and took from it without its owner's permission so it was unlawful, then he bought it so it became lawful."
"2073","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from his father, from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, concerning a man who commits immorality with a woman then marries her, he said: They remain two fornicators as long as they stay together."
"2074","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and Dawud from al-Sha'bi, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: They are two fornicators as long as they lie together."
"2075","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif informed us, from Sulayman ibn al-Jahm al-Kindi, from al-Bara' ibn 'Azib, he said: They are two fornicators as long as they stay together."
"2076","Sa'id narrated to us, Dawud ibn 'Ulbah narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, concerning a man who commits immorality with a woman then marries her, she said: Unlawful until the Day of Resurrection."
"2077","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, that he was asked about that, and he recited this verse: {And He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons evil deeds, and He knows what they do}."
"2078","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: A man came to 'Alqamah and said to him: A man committed immorality with a woman, may he marry her? He said: Yes. And he recited to him this verse: {And He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons evil deeds, and He knows what they do}."
"2079","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Janab al-Kalbi informed us, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from his father, he said: We disputed over the reading of this phrase: {And He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons evil deeds, and He knows what they do} or {you do}, so I went to Ibn Mas'ud to ask him about that, and while I was with him a visitor came to him and said: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, a man attained something unlawful from a woman, then they both repented and set things right, may he marry her? So 'Abd Allah recited: {And He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons evil deeds, and He knows what they do}."
"2080","Sa'id narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah said, Abu Janab Yahya ibn Abi Hayyah al-Kalbi narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from his father, from 'Abd Allah, the like of it, and he said: Let him marry her."
"2081","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, concerning a man who commits immorality with a woman then marries her, he said: He has more right to her."
"2082","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Attab narrated to us, he said: Husayf informed us, from Mujahid, he said: If a man commits zina with a woman, it is not proper for him to marry her."
"2083","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, that Abu al-Sha'tha' ordered him to ask 'Ikrimah about a man who committed immorality with a woman, then saw her nursing a slave girl, is it proper for him to marry the girl? So I asked him, and he said: No."
"2084","Chapter on a man who frees his slave girl then marries her. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed his slave girl Safiyyah bint Huyayy ibn Akhtab and married her, and it was said to Anas: What did he give her as dower? He said: He gave her herself as dower; he made her freeing her dower."
"2085","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, made her freeing her dower, and freed those taken captive of her people of Banu al-Mustaliq."
"2086","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: Juwayriyah said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your wives boast over me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not marry you. He said: Did I not magnify your dower? Did I not free forty of your people?"
"2087","Sa'id narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three are given their rewards twice: a man of the People of the Book who believed in what 'Isa brought and in what Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought, and a slave who obeyed his Lord and obeyed his masters, and a man who freed a slave girl then married her."
"2088","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three are given their rewards twice: a man who has a slave girl and frees her then marries her, and a slave who obeys Allah, mighty and majestic, and renders his master's right, and a believer of the People of the Book."
"2089","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from 'Amir al-Sha'bi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning one who frees his slave girl then marries her, he has two rewards."
"2090","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Hayy al-Hamdani informed us, he said: I was with al-Sha'bi when a man of the people of Khurasan came to him and said: O Abu 'Amr, those among the people of Khurasan in our direction say concerning a man who frees his slave girl then marries her that he is like one riding his sacrificial camel. So al-Sha'bi said: Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa informed me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three are given their reward twice: a man of the People of the Book who believed in his prophet, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached him and he believed in him then followed him, so he has two rewards, and an owned slave who renders Allah's right and his master's right upon him, so he has two rewards, and a man who had a slave girl whom he fed and fed well, then disciplined her and disciplined well, then freed her and married her, so he has two rewards. Then al-Sha'bi said to the Khurasani: Take it for nothing, for a man used to travel to Medina for what is less than it."
"2091","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salih ibn Hayy, from al-Sha'bi, he said: A man of the people of Khurasan asked him and said to him: O Abu 'Amr, we say that one who frees his slave girl then marries her is like one riding his sacrificial camel. He said: Abu Burdah informed me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any man who had a slave girl and taught her and taught her well, and disciplined her and disciplined her well, then freed her and married her, he has two rewards, and any slave who renders Allah's right and his master's right, he has two rewards, and any man of the People of the Book who was a believer then believed in the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he has two rewards. Then al-Sha'bi said: I have given it to you for nothing, for a man used to travel to Medina for what is easier than this."
"2092","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Ibn 'Umar, that he used to say concerning a man who marries his freed woman: He is like one riding his sacrificial camel. He said: And Ibrahim and our companions saw no harm in that, and most beloved of that to them was that they make her freeing her dower."
"2093","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who frees a slave girl for Allah, mighty and majestic, then marries her, he said: Ibn 'Umar used to say: He is like one riding his sacrificial camel. He said: And most liked of that to our companions was that they make her freeing her dower."
"2094","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that he liked to give her something along with her freeing, whatever it was."
"2095","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he saw no harm in making her freeing her dower."
"2096","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, and Mughirah from Ibrahim, and Yunus from al-Hasan, he said: And 'Abd al-Malik from 'Ata', that they saw no harm in that."
"2097","Sa'id narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: He should not say: I have freed you and married you, but let him say: I have freed you on condition that I marry you."
"2098","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman informed us, he said: I heard 'Ata' say: If a man says to his slave girl: I have freed you and married you, she is his wife, and if he says: I will free you and marry you, then he frees her, then if she wishes she marries him, and if she wishes she does not marry him."
"2099","Chapter on a man who marries a woman then dies without fixing a dower for her. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from 'Abd Khayr, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said concerning a widow to whom no dower was fixed, he said: She has the inheritance, and she has no dower."
"2100","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Hakam, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, the like of that."
"2101","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, that he said: She has the inheritance and upon her is the waiting period, and she has no dower."
"2102","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Ibn 'Umar married a son of his to the daughter of his brother 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar, and his son was small at the time and he did not fix a dower for her, and the boy lived some time then died, so the girl's maternal uncle disputed with Ibn 'Umar before Zayd ibn Thabit, and Ibn 'Umar said to Zayd: I married my son while I was telling myself I would do good for him, but he died before that, and he did not fix a dower for the girl. So Zayd said: She has the inheritance if the boy had wealth, and upon her is the waiting period, and she has no dower."
"2103","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Dawud, from 'Amir al-Sha'bi, that Ibn 'Umar and Zayd ibn Thabit said concerning a man who married a woman and did not fix a dower for her then died, they said: She has the inheritance, and she has no dower. Masruq said: There was never an inheritance except that a dower was before it."
"2104","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: This view of the people of Medina was mentioned to Masruq, and Masruq said: There was never an inheritance except that a dower was before it."
"2105","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Nafi', he said: Ibn 'Umar married his son to his brother's daughter, and the girl died before a dower was fixed for her, so her mother asked for her dower, and Ibn 'Umar said: She has no dower. So they disputed before Zayd ibn Thabit, and he said: She has no dower, and she has the inheritance."
"2106","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, that he was approached concerning a man who married a woman and did not fix a dower for her, then died before consummating with her, so they came to Ibn Mas'ud, and he said: Seek, perhaps you will find a precedent in that. So they came to Ibn Mas'ud and said: We have sought and found nothing. So Ibn Mas'ud said: I speak in it by my opinion; if it is correct it is from Allah, mighty and majestic: I see for her the dower of her peers, neither diminished nor excessive, and upon her is the waiting period, and she has the inheritance. So Abu Sinan al-Ashja'i stood and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged for a woman of ours called Barwa' bint Washiq with the like of what you said. So 'Abd Allah rejoiced at his agreement with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2107","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid and Dawud informed us, all of them from al-Sha'bi, from 'Abd Allah, with the like of that, except that they said: Ma'qil ibn Sinan al-Ashja'i stood and said: I bear witness upon the unlettered Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he judged with the like of what you judged. Hushaym said: And by it we take."
"2108","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Kufi narrated to us, from Mazidah ibn Jabir, that 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The word of a bedouin of Ashja' is not accepted against the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"2109","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, Zakariyya informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: A grave chapter of divorce: if the woman inherits, she observes the waiting period."
"2110","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning a woman whose husband died without fixing a dower for her, he said: She has the like of the dower of her peers."
"2111","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, he said: 'Ata' al-Khurasani narrated to me, he said: 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz wrote to the people concerning a man who marries a woman then divorces her before consummating with her and before fixing for her that she has half the dower, and she has no waiting period, and she has no inheritance."
"2112","Chapter on what has come concerning a man who marries a woman then she dies before he consummates with her or he divorces her, is it proper for him to marry her mother. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym and Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who marries a woman then she dies before - I think he said: consummating with her - may he marry her mother? He said: Shurayh, when approached in that, used to say: Go to Banu Shamkh and ask them about that."
"2113","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'd ibn Iyas, concerning a man who married a woman of Banu Shamkh, then saw her mother and she pleased him, so he went to Ibn Mas'ud and said: I married a woman and did not consummate with her, then her mother pleased me, so shall I divorce the woman and marry her mother? He said: Yes. So he divorced her and married her mother, then 'Abd Allah came to Medina and asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: It is not proper. Then he came and went to Banu Shamkh and said: Where is the man who married the mother of the woman who was with him? They said: Here he is. He said: Let him separate from her. They said: How, when she has borne him children? He said: Even if she did, let him separate from her, for she is unlawful by Allah, mighty and majestic."
"2114","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, that he was asked about the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: {And the mothers of your wives}, and Ibn 'Abbas said: It is unqualified, so release what Allah released, and follow what Allah, mighty and majestic, clarified. He said: He permitted the stepdaughter if he had not consummated with her mother, and disliked the mother in every case."
"2115","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, he said: It is in the mushaf of 'Abd Allah: (And your stepdaughters who are in your laps from your wives with whose mothers you consummated; if you have not consummated with them, there is no sin upon you). Hushaym said: I do not know whether it was mentioned in the hadith, or he said: such."
"2116","Sa'id narrated to us, Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, he said: 'Ikrimah was asked about a man who married a woman and did not consummate with her until he died, or he divorced her, may his son marry her? He said: Concerning it Dawud killed his son Adhin. [Flag: wording obscure/garbled in source]"
"2117","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he permitted the stepdaughter if he had not consummated with her mother, and disliked the mother in every case."
"2118","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: If he marries the mother of his wife while he had consummated with his wife, he separates from both together, and if it was the sister, he stays with his wife and does not approach her until he clears the womb of the other, then when he has cleared her womb he returns to his wife."
"2119","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar informed us, from 'Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara' ibn 'Azib, he said: My uncle al-Harith ibn 'Amr passed by me, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had tied a banner for him, so I turned to him and said: Where has the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent you? He said: He sent me to a man who married his father's wife, and ordered me to strike his neck."
"2120","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahm, from al-Bara' ibn 'Azib, he said: While I was in a place, a company of riders with a banner was raised before us, and they came until they brought out a man and struck his neck, so we said: What is this? They said: This is a man who wedded his father's wife last night."
"2121","Chapter on what has come concerning the brother's daughter through nursing. Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu 'Awn, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from 'Ali, upon him peace, he said: I asked him about the brother's daughter through nursing, and 'Ali said: I mentioned Hamzah's daughter in marriage to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: She is the daughter of my brother through nursing."
"2122","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, suggested to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he marry Hamzah's daughter, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hamzah was my brother through nursing."
"2123","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: Hamzah's daughter was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they mentioned her beauty, so he said: Hamzah was my brother through nursing."
"2124","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed, from al-Hasan, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, if you married Hamzah's daughter? He said: Hamzah was my brother through nursing, and there is prohibited through nursing what is prohibited through lineage."
"2125","Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: 'Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry the daughter of your uncle Hamzah? For she is among the most beautiful girls of Quraysh. He said: She is the daughter of my brother through nursing, and Allah has prohibited through nursing what He prohibited through lineage."
"2126","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prohibited through nursing is what is prohibited through lineage."
"2127","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm, from 'A'ishah, that she said: Prohibited through nursing is what is prohibited through birth."
"2128","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri and Hisham ibn 'Urwah - Sufyan said: I heard it from them both together - from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: My uncle Aflah ibn Abi Qu'ays came seeking permission from me after the veil was imposed upon us, and I refused to permit him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, and I mentioned that to him, so he said: He is your uncle, so let him enter upon you. I said: Only the woman nursed me, the man did not nurse me. He said: May your hands be dusty, so let him enter upon you."
"2129","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, he said: 'A'ishah said: O son of my sister, prohibited through nursing is what is prohibited through lineage."
"2130","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from 'Urwah, he said: 'A'ishah said to me: My uncle through nursing came to me after the veil was imposed upon us, seeking permission from me, and I said: By Allah, I shall not permit him until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) comes, so when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came I asked his permission, and he said: He may enter upon you, for he is your uncle. And 'A'ishah used to say: Prohibited through nursing is what is prohibited through birth."
"2131","Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn Mansur informed, he said: I said to al-Qasim ibn Muhammad: My father's wife nursed a girl of strangers with the milk of my brothers, do you see that I may marry her? He said: No, your father is her father. Then he narrated the hadith of Abu Qu'ays, and said: Abu Qu'ays came to 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, seeking permission from her, and she did not permit him, so when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, 'A'ishah said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Qu'ays came seeking permission from me, and I did not permit him. He said: He is your uncle, so let him enter upon you. I said: Only a woman nursed me, the man did not nurse me? He said: He is your uncle, so let him enter upon you. He said: And I asked Tawus, and he said the like of the first ones' saying, and I asked 'Ata', and he said the like of that, and I asked al-Hasan, and he said the like of the first ones' saying. And I asked Mujahid, and he said: The jurists differed in it, so I say nothing in it. And I asked Ibn Sirin, and he said the like of Mujahid's saying, and I asked Yusuf ibn Mahak, and he mentioned the hadith of Abu Qu'ays."
"2132","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to dislike the milk of the sire."
"2133","Sa'id narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that he disliked the milk of the sire."
"2134","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Sabrah al-Hamdani informed us, that he heard al-Sha'bi dislike it."
"2135","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that he saw no harm in the milk of the sire, and that Mujahid disliked it."
"2136","Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, that he saw no harm in the milk of the sire."
"2137","Sa'id narrated to us, Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Bukayr ibn 'Abd Allah, from Abu Qilabah, that he saw no harm in it."
"2138","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Husayn, freedman of Qudamah ibn Maz'un, informed us, that Salim ibn 'Abd Allah married a son of his to a sister from his father through nursing."
"2139","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Aflah ibn Humayd informed me, he said: I said to al-Qasim, meaning Ibn Muhammad: So-and-so of the family of Banu Farwah wants to marry a boy to his sister from his father through nursing. He said: There is no harm in that."
"2140","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Rabi'ah and Yahya ibn Sa'id and 'Amr ibn 'Ubayd Allah and Aflah ibn Humayd narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: Whoever was nursed by the daughters of Abu Bakr would enter upon 'A'ishah, and whoever was nursed by the wives of the sons of Abu Bakr would not enter upon her."
"2141","Sa'id narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from his father, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while a man was with me, and it weighed heavily upon him until I recognized anger in his face, I said: O Messenger of Allah, he is my brother through nursing. He said: Look to your sisters through nursing, for nursing is only from hunger."
"2142","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn 'Ali, he said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn did not see the Mothers of the Believers. Ibn 'Abbas said: Their seeing them is lawful. [Flag: verb ambiguous in source: see vs. hold opinion]"
"2143","Sa'id narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amr ibn al-Sharid, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: A man came to him and said: I have a wife and a slave girl, this one nursed a boy, and this one nursed a girl, is it proper for the boy to marry the girl? He said: It is not proper, the sire is one."
"2144","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi narrated to me, he said: My uncle Iyas ibn 'Amir narrated to me, he said: 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me: Do not marry one whom your father's mother nursed, nor your son's wife, nor your brother's wife."
"2145","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn 'Uqbah, that he asked 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr about nursing, he said: 'A'ishah did not consider one suck nor two sucks anything, short of ten feedings onward. Then I asked him about nursing after weaning, he said: That is only food he ate, it is nothing. Then I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib about nursing, and Sa'id said: I do not say as Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn al-Zubayr say. I said: How did they say? He said: They said: One suck and two sucks do not prohibit. I said: How do you say? He said: If a drop entered his belly and he knows that, she is unlawful to him. I said: What about nursing after weaning? He said: That is only food he ate, it is nothing."
"2146","Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suck and two sucks do not prohibit."
"2147","Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us, from Abu al-Khalil, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Umm al-Fadl, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my house, and a bedouin came and said: I had a wife, and I married another wife over her, and my first wife claimed she nursed my other wife once or twice, or one or two imlajah. He said: One or two imlajah do not prohibit. Or he said: One or two sucklings."
"2148","Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Hayyan ibn 'Umayr, he said: Ibn 'Abbas said: Seven by marriage, seven by lineage, and prohibited through nursing is what is prohibited through lineage."
"2149","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: Whatever is in the first two years, it prohibits, even if a suck, and whatever is after the two years is nothing."
"2150","Sa'id narrated to us, Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah and Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Whatever is by pouring or snuff in the first two years, it prohibits, and whatever is after, it does not prohibit. Hushaym said: The two years."
"2151","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from 'Abd Allah, he said: There is no nursing except what is in the first two years, what strengthens the bone and grows the flesh."
"2152","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu 'Umar al-Shaybani, that a man confined the milk in his wife's breast, and began sucking it then spitting it out, then it entered his throat, so he came to al-Ash'ari, and al-Ash'ari said: Do not approach your wife. So it was said: Go to Ibn Mas'ud. So he came to 'Abd Allah and told him what al-Ash'ari said, he said: This is only wholesome, it is not unlawful."
"2153","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Quran came down with ten known sucklings, then they were five."
"2154","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: There is no nursing except what is in the cradle."
"2155","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: There is no nursing except what opens the intestines."
"2156","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah say: Al-'ayfah does not prohibit. It was said: What is al-'ayfah? He said: A woman confines the milk in her breast, then nurses a neighbor's child with it."
"2157","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: There is no nursing except what is in the first two years."
"2158","Sa'id narrated to us, 'Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, Husayf informed us, from Tawus, he said: One suck and two sucks prohibit."
"2159","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Umayyah, from Tawus, he said: What they then said: One suckling prohibits."
"2160","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: One suckling of nursing prohibits."
"2161","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn 'Umar was asked about something of nursing, he said: We know only that Allah, mighty and majestic, prohibited the sister through nursing. I said: The Commander of the Believers Ibn al-Zubayr says: One suckling and two sucklings, nor one suck nor two sucks, do not prohibit. Ibn 'Umar said: Allah's decree is better than your decree and the decree of the Commander of the Believers with you."
"2162","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn 'Umar, from 'Umar, he said: There is no nursing except what is in childhood."
"2163","Sa'id narrated to us, Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Hakim, that a man asked his wife for water on a hot day, she said: I gave you to drink from my milk. So he asked 'Umar ibn al-Khattab about that, and he said: Leave her, there is no good for you in her, and if you keep her, hurt her back."
"2164","Sa'id narrated to us, Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that a man whose wife gave him her milk by pouring or by snuff, so they came to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and he said: She has become unlawful to him. Then they came to 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, and he said: There is no nursing after the two years; nursing is only what grows the flesh and strengthens the bone. Abu Musa said: Do not ask me - or: you should not ask me - about anything while this scholar is among you."
"2165","Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah al-Laythi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, he said: I asked Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, and Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, and 'Ata' ibn Yasar about the milk of the sire, and all of them saw no harm in it."
"2166","Sa'id narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prohibited through nursing is what is prohibited through birth."
"2167","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from 'Uqbah ibn al-Harith, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I married the daughter of Abu Ihab, and a woman claimed she nursed us. So he turned away from him, then he came to him from the other side and he turned away from him, then he came to him from before his face, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, she is black. He said: How, since it has been said."
"2168","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: The testimony of one woman is valid in nursing, even if she was black."
"2169","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla and al-Hajjaj informed us, from 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab was approached concerning a woman who testified about a man and his wife that she nursed them both, and he said: No, until two men, or a man and two women, testify."
"2170","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Wahb ibn 'Uqbah - born in the time of 'Uthman - that a woman testified about nursing and said: I nursed a man and his wife. So 'Uthman ibn 'Affan said: She swears at the Ka'bah. And when she was pressed upon that, she retracted."
"2171","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, and Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, concerning a woman when she testifies about a man and his wife that she nursed them, he said once: If she was pleasing, and said once: If she was just, she is made to swear by Allah that she nursed them, and if she swears the two are separated. Hushaym said: And it is not acted upon."
"2172","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in a man seeking a Jewish woman and a Christian woman and an immoral woman to nurse his child."
"2173","Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mukhbir informed us, from Ibrahim, the like of it, except that he did not mention the immoral woman."
"2174","Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Habib, from a man of Kinanah - I think, 'Utwarī - he said: I sat with Ibn 'Umar, and he said: Are you of the sons of so-and-so? I said: No, but they nursed me. He said: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab say: Milk is confused upon him. [Flag: terse/obscure in source]"
"2175","Chapter on what has come concerning one who gives a dower secretly and announces more than that. Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh, concerning one who gives a dower secretly and announces more than that, that he validated the secret and nullified the public. Hushaym said: And it is the view with us."
"2176","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: 'The secret (dower) is valid and the publicized (addition) is void.'"
"2177","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from Abu Awn Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Thaqafi, from Shurayh, the same as that."
"2178","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn and Ismail ibn Salim and Abd al-Salam, freedman of Quraysh, informed us that they heard al-Shabi saying: 'The publicized is acted upon.'"
"2179","Said narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn, from Amir al-Shabi, who said: 'The publicized is acted upon.'"
"2180","Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from al-Shabi, who said: 'The publicized is acted upon.' Hushaym said: Ibn Abi Layla said: 'He takes by the publicized.'"
"2181","Chapter on combining a man's daughter and his wife (in marriage). Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that he used to dislike combining a man's daughter and his wife."
"2182","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that he saw no harm in that."
"2183","Said narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, who said: al-Hasan and Muhammad ibn Sirin were asked about a man marrying a man's wife and his daughter by another woman; al-Hasan disliked it, while Muhammad ibn Sirin saw no harm in it, and said: Jabal, a man of Egypt, did it."
"2184","Said narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, who said: 'I was sitting with al-Hasan when he was asked about it and he disliked it. One of the people said: O Abu Said, do you see anything (wrong) between them? He looked, then said: I see nothing between them.'"
"2185","Said narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and Sufyan, from Amr ibn Dinar, that Abdullah ibn Safwan combined a man's wife and his daughter (in marriage)."
"2186","Said narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, that Abdullah ibn Safwan married a Thaqafi man's wife and his daughter."
"2187","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Qutham, freedman of Banu Hashim, that Abdullah ibn Jafar combined the daughter of Ali and his Nahshalite wife (in marriage)."
"2188","Said narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Qutham, freedman of the family of al-Abbas, who said: Abdullah ibn Jafar combined Layla bint Masud al-Nahshaliyyah, who had been the wife of Ali, and Umm Kulthum bint Ali, daughter of Fatimah bint Rasul Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and they were both his wives."
"2189","Chapter on a man who marries a woman and enters upon her while slave girls are with her, then falls upon one of them. Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he was asked about a man who married a girl and entered upon her while slave girls were with her; he took one and she said: I am not your wife, so he left her; then he took another and she said: I am not your wife, so he left her; then he took another and she said: I am not your wife, and he said: are you resisting me? Then he had intercourse with her, and lo, she was not his wife. Ibrahim said: 'She gets the dower, and the hadd punishment is averted from him due to his ignorance.'"
"2190","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, who said: 'Whoever has intercourse with a private part out of ignorance, the hadd is averted from him, and he owes the indemnity (uqr).'"
"2191","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, about a man found with a woman having intercourse with her, and he said: she is my wife, and she said: he is my husband. He said: 'Proof of that is demanded, otherwise the hadd is applied to them both; if this were accepted, no hadd would ever be applied to a fornicator.'"
"2192","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: we were with Humayd al-Tawil and al-Harith al-Ghanawi, and they discussed this chapter. Humayd said: 'They are both asked for proof, otherwise the hadd is applied to them.' Al-Harith al-Ghanawi said: their word is accepted, and there is no hadd upon them. While we were thus, Ibn Shubrumah came; Humayd said to al-Harith: this is Ibn Shubrumah, and he is (arbiter) between me and you. Ibn Shubrumah came and sat, Humayd asked him, and Ibn Shubrumah gave the opinion of Ibrahim."
"2193","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Shubah informed us, who said: I heard al-Hakam and Hammad saying: 'Their word is accepted.' Hushaym said: and that is the opinion."
"2194","Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sumayt, from al-Sadusi, who said: 'I proposed to a woman, and they said to me: we will not marry you until you divorce your wife thrice. I said: I have divorced thrice, so they married me to her. Then they looked and found my wife still with me. They said: did you not divorce thrice? I said: yes; I had so-and-so daughter of so-and-so and I divorced her, and so-and-so daughter of so-and-so and I divorced her, but this one I did not divorce. Then I came to Shaqiq ibn Majzaah ibn Thawr as he was about to go to Uthman ibn Affan as a delegate, and said to him: ask the Commander of the Faithful about this. He went to him and asked him, and Uthman said: (it depends on) his intention.' [Flag: chain wording compressed; print-collation note stripped]"
"2195","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Shabi, that he was asked about a man who proposed to some people, and they married him on condition that if he has a wife then the dower of their kinswoman is two thousand, and if he has no wife then her dower is one thousand; so they married him on that, then they found he had a wife. Al-Shabi said: 'She gets the lesser of the two dowers.'"
"2196","Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Tawus, who said: 'If a man has a son, and he has a wife who has a daughter by another man, and his son is by another woman, there is no harm in the son marrying the wife's daughter if she was born before the father married her; but if after, he disliked it.' Mujahid saw no harm in it before or after. Abu Uthman said: the opinion is what Mujahid said."
"2197","Chapter on one who divorces before he owns (i.e. before marriage). Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Amir al-Ahwal informed us, Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that Rasul Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There is no vow for the son of Adam in what he does not own, no manumission for him in what he does not own, and no divorce for him in what he does not own.'"
"2198","Said narrated to us, Abu Alqamah al-Farwi narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Hakim ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to me, who said: Amr ibn Shuayb came to us and I asked him. He said: my father offered me a woman to marry me to her, and I refused to marry her, and said: she is divorced outright the day I marry her. Then I regretted, so I came to Madinah and asked Said ibn al-Musayyib and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, and they said: Rasul Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There is no divorce except after marriage.'"
"2199","Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: 'Zihar and divorce before ownership are nothing.'"
"2200","Said narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Said ibn Amr ibn Sulaym, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that a man said: if I marry so-and-so, she is upon me like my mother's back. Then he married her, and asked Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: 'Do not approach her until you expiate the expiation of zihar.'"
"2201","Said narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Shurayh, who said: 'There is no divorce except after marriage.'"
"2202","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah informed us, who said: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that he was asked about a man who said: if I marry so-and-so she is divorced. He said: 'It is nothing; there is no divorce except after ownership.'"
"2203","Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from a man, from Abu al-Shaatha, who said: 'Divorce is after marriage, and manumission after ownership.'"
"2204","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ashath ibn Sawwar informed us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: 'There is no divorce except after marriage, and no manumission except after ownership.'"
"2205","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ubaydah narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Rawah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: 'There is no divorce except after marriage.'"
"2206","Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abi al-Mughirah, who said: I asked Said ibn Jubayr and Ali ibn Husayn about divorce before marriage, and they considered it nothing."
"2207","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Juwaybir informed us, from al-Dahhak, who said: al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah al-Hilali informed me, who said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: 'There is no continuous fasting (wisal), no suckling after weaning, no orphanhood after puberty, no silence (as worship) a day till the night, and no divorce except after marriage.'"
"2208","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur and Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: 'There is no divorce except after ownership.'"
"2209","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said and Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, who said: 'There is no divorce except after marriage.'"
"2210","Said narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, who said: a man came to Ali ibn Husayn and said: I said: the day I marry so-and-so she is divorced. Then he recited this verse: (O you who believe, when you marry believing women then divorce them before you touch them). Ali ibn Husayn said: 'I see no divorce except after marriage.'"
"2211","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, al-Ajlah informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, who said: a man came to Ali ibn Husayn and said: what do you say about a man who said: if I marry so-and-so she is divorced? He said: 'It is nothing; Allah began with marriage before divorce, then said: (O you who believe, when you marry believing women then divorce them). Allah began with marriage before divorce, and his statement is nothing.'"
"2212","Said narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, who said: when he says: 'Every woman I marry is upon me like my mother's back,' he expiates for the first woman he marries; and when he says: if I marry so-and-so she is upon me like my mother's back, and he marries her, let him not approach her until he expiates."
"2213","Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Salih al-Asadi narrated to us, who said: a man came to Ibrahim and said: I swore by divorcing the wife of so-and-so; I said: I will not marry her until I go out to Isbahan. Ibrahim said to him: 'Go out to Isbahan, then marry her afterwards.'"
"2214","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid informed us, Udayy ibn Kab narrated to me, who said: a man came to Said ibn al-Musayyib and said: what do you say about a man who said: if I marry so-and-so she is divorced? Said said to him: how much would you dower her? The man said to him: he has not married her yet, so how would he dower her? Said said to him: then how does he divorce what he has not married?"
"2215","Said narrated to us, Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to us, who said: I asked Ata and Tawus and Said ibn al-Musayyib, and they said the same as that; and I asked Mujahid and he disliked it."
"2216","Said narrated to us, Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, Khusayf informed us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that he swore concerning a woman that if he marries her she is divorced; then he married her. Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, then governor of Madinah, was informed of that and sent to him: 'It reached me that you swore concerning such-and-such.' He said: yes. He said: will you not let her go? He said: no. So Umar left him and did not separate them."
"2217","Said narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, who said: I asked Mansur ibn Zadham about a man to whom a woman was mentioned and he said: 'If I marry her she is divorced.' He said: al-Hasan used to consider it nothing."
"2218","Said narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, who said: I asked Abu Hashim, and he said: 'She is divorced; so what does he want (i.e. it counts)?' [Flag: terse ruling]"
"2219","Said narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, that a man said about a little slave girl: if I marry her she is divorced. She grew up and he desired her, so he married her; then he felt scruple about that and said to me: ask for me about that. So I met Amir al-Shabi and asked him; he said: go to Ibrahim, for I left him at such-and-such place, ask him, then come back to me and tell me what he says. He said: so I met him and asked him, and he reported from Alqamah or al-Aswad, who said: Abdullah said: 'She is as he said.' He said: so I returned to Amir and told him, and he said: he spoke the truth; it is as he said. Then I met the husband and told him what they said; so he came to his wife and told her that she has more right to herself, then he proposed to her and married her."
"2220","Said narrated to us, Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, Juwaybir narrated to us, from al-Dahhak, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: when a man says: every woman I marry is divorced, he said: 'It is nothing unless he sets a time limit.'"
"2221","Said narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, about a man who said: 'If I marry so-and-so, or he said: from Banu so-and-so, she is divorced; if he marries then she is divorced. But if he says: every woman I marry is divorced, it is nothing.'"
"2222","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he said about a man who said: 'Every woman I marry is divorced.' He said: 'It is nothing; this is a man who forbade chaste women to himself. But when he says: if I marry so-and-so she is divorced, and he marries her, then she is divorced as he said.' [Flag: one phrase obscure in print; collation note stripped]"
"2223","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: 'When he names her or her lineage, or names a town, or sets a time, it is as he said.'"
"2224","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Shabi, that he used to say the same as that."
"2225","Said narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, and al-Shabi, about a man who said: every woman he marries is divorced. They said: 'It is nothing; he forbade chaste women (to himself).' But when he says: every woman he marries from Banu so-and-so, or from a town, or a tribe, she is divorced as he said."
"2226","Said narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muslim and Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, about a man who said to his wife: 'If I marry a woman while you are with me, she is divorced.' [Flag: report breaks off here in source]"
"2227","Said narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muslim, from al-Shabi, about a man who said: every woman he marries from Banu Asad is divorced. He said: 'He may turn to others.'"
"2228","Said narrated to us, Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Amr ibn Muhammad and Salim ibn Abdillah, who said: 'When he says: every woman he marries is divorced, it is as he said.'"
"2229","Said narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: a man said to a woman: if I marry her she is upon him like his mother's back. He said: 'He expiates if he marries her before he touches her: that is what you are admonished by.'"
"2230","Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ubaydah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, who was asked about a man who married a free woman and a slave girl in one contract. He said: 'The marriage of the free woman is confirmed and the marriage of the slave girl is dropped.'"
"2231","Said narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, that his father used to say: 'Every divorce or manumission before ownership is void.'"
"2232","Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, who said: a woman came to al-Shabi and said: I swore to my husband that I would not marry after him, with stern oaths; what do you see? He said: 'I see that we begin with what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, made lawful before your unlawful.' (End of the Book of Marriage.)"
"2233","The Book of Divorce. Said narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, about His saying, Mighty and Majestic: (then divorce them for their waiting period): that he divorce her without intercourse, then wait until she menstruates one menstruation then becomes pure, then wait until she menstruates one menstruation then becomes pure; if he wishes to take her back, he takes her back."
"2234","Said informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: Abdullah said: 'Divorce for the waiting period is that a man divorce his wife while she is pure without intercourse.'"
"2235","Said informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: Ibn Abbas used to recite: (then divorce them before their waiting period)."
"2236","Said informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Mujahid saying: (then divorce them before their waiting period). Sufyan said: I never heard Ibn Jurayj say 'I heard Mujahid' about anything except this."
"2237","Said informed us, Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Ibn Sirin, who said: 'Divorce for the waiting period is that he divorce her while she is pure without intercourse, or with an evident pregnancy.'"
"2238","Said informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Khalid and Ibn Awn informed us, from Ibn Sirin, who said: 'Divorce for the waiting period is that a man divorce his wife while she is pure without intercourse, or with an evident pregnancy.'"
"2239","Said informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman informed us, who said: I was with Said ibn Jubayr when a man of Basra came to him and said: 'I have been afflicted with a grave matter.' He said: what is it? He said: my wife, my cousin; I think of divorcing her until I see my tongue moved with that, until I put my hand over my mouth fearing that speech of divorcing her may slip out. Said said: will you obey? He said: I asked you only wanting to obey you. He said: divorce is not there; the divorce Allah commanded is that a man divorce his wife while she is pure without intercourse, and that he call witnesses to her divorce and to her return if he wishes that; that is the divorce Allah commanded. [Flag: one word uncertain in print; collation note stripped]"
"2240","Chapter on transgression in divorce. Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, who said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, who said: a man came to Abdullah and said: 'I divorced my wife ninety-nine times.' Abdullah said: what did they say to you? He said: they said: she is forbidden to you. Abdullah said: they wanted to burden you; she is separated from you by three, and the rest is transgression."
"2241","Said informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, who said: a man came to Ibn Abbas and said: 'His uncle divorced his wife thrice and more.' He said: 'You disobeyed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, your wife is separated from you, and you did not fear Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so that He would make a way out for you.'"
"2242","Said informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: al-Amash informed us, from Imran ibn al-Harith al-Sulami, who said: a man came to Ibn Abbas and said: 'His uncle divorced thrice and regretted.' He said: 'Your uncle disobeyed Allah so He made him regret, and obeyed Satan so He made no way out for him.' He said: what if I marry her without his knowledge, will she return to him? He said: 'Whoever deceives Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Allah deceives him.'"
"2243","Said informed us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, who said: I was with Abdullah ibn Umar when a man called Muhr, freedman of the family of Abu Namir, came to him and said: 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, he divorced his wife a hundred times.' He said: what is your name? He said: Muhr. He said: rather you are Muhayr (little Muhr); three are taken from you, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will reckon you for ninety-seven on the Day of Resurrection."
"2244","Said informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: 'You had deliberation in divorce, but you hastened your deliberation; and we have enforced upon you what you hastened of that.'"
"2245","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Abu Hurrah informed us, from al-Hasan, about a man who divorces his wife thrice in one word. He said: Umar said: 'If only we carried them upon the Book of Allah.' Then he said: 'No, rather we bind them with what they bound themselves.'"
"2246","Said narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from al-Hasan, that Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Abu Musa al-Ashari: 'I considered making, when a man divorces his wife thrice in one sitting, it count as one; but people burdened themselves, so bind every soul with what it bound itself: whoever says to his wife: you are unlawful to me, she is unlawful; whoever says to his wife: you are separated, she is separated; and whoever says: you are divorced thrice, it is three.'"
"2247","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, that he used to dislike a man divorcing his wife thrice in one word, saying: 'Let him divorce her once, then leave her until the waiting period ends.'"
"2248","Said informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Abu Awn informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that he saw no harm in divorcing thrice."
"2249","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Zakariyya informed us, from al-Shabi, who said: a man came to him and said he wishes relief from his wife. He said: 'Then divorce her thrice if you wish.'"
"2250","Said narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Anas ibn Malik, about one who divorced his wife thrice before consummating with her. He said: 'She is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.' And Umar, when a man who divorced his wife thrice was brought to him, would hurt his back."
"2251","Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Shaqiq, who heard Anas ibn Malik saying about a man who divorces his wife thrice before consummating with her. He said: 'It is three; she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband. And Umar, when he was brought to him, would hurt him.'"
"2252","Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri - Sufyan said: I think - from Abu Salamah, that Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayrah and Abdullah ibn Amr said about one who divorces his wife thrice before consummating with her: 'She is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.'"
"2253","Said narrated to us, Sufyan and Hammad ibn Zayd and Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, about one who divorced his wife thrice before consummating with her. He said: 'She is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.'"
"2254","Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata and Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: 'When a virgin is divorced thrice, it is one.'"
"2255","Said narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Ibrahim, about a man who says to his wife, whom he has not consummated with: you are divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced. He said: 'She is separated by the first, the two are nothing; but if he divorces her thrice in one breath, she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.'"
"2256","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, about one who divorced his wife thrice without consummating with her. He said: 'She is not lawful to him until she marries another husband. But when he says: you are divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced, she is separated by the first, and the other two are nothing.'"
"2257","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Mutarrif informed us, from al-Hakam, that he said: when he says: 'She is divorced thrice, she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband; but when he says: you are divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced, she is separated by the first, and the other two are nothing.' It was said to him: from whom is this, O Abu Abdillah? He said: 'From Ali and Abdullah and Zayd ibn Thabit.'"
"2258","Said narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, about a man who says to his wife: you are divorced thrice before consummating with her. He said: 'If he uttered them together, she is not lawful to him; but if he uttered them successively, she is separated by the first, and the two are nothing.'"
"2259","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Mughirah informed us, who said: 'When he says: you are divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced: if it was continuous speech, she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband; but if he says: you are divorced, then falls silent, then says: you are divorced, you are divorced, she is separated by the first, and the other two are nothing.'"
"2260","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Mughirah informed us, from al-Shabi, from Abdullah ibn Maqil al-Muzani, that he said: 'When it was continuous, she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.'"
"2261","Said narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, about a man who divorced his wife before consummating with her with a continuous divorce, saying: you are divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced. He said: 'She is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.'"
"2262","Said narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdillah and Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Azrah, from Ibn Masud, about a man who divorced his wife thrice before consummating with her. He said: 'She is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.'"
"2263","Said narrated to us, Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, who said: Khusayf informed us, from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam, from Ibn Masud, about a man who divorces his wife all together without having consummated with her. He said: 'It is three; but if he divorces once, then seconds and thirds, it does not fall upon her because she was separated by the first.'"
"2264","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Abu Bishr informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, who said: 'When he says: you are divorced thrice before consummating with her, she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.'"
"2265","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan, that he said about one who divorced his wife thrice before consummating with her: 'May his nose be rubbed in dust; it reached its limit: (she is not lawful) until she marries another husband.'"
"2266","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he said: 'After that, if he wishes, he may propose to her.'"
"2267","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Mughirah and Husayn informed us, from Ibrahim, who said: 'She is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.'"
"2268","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from al-Shabi, that he said that also."
"2269","Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, who said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, that he was asked about a man who divorced his wife a thousand times before consummating with her. He said: 'She is separated from him by three, and the rest is disobedience.'"
"2270","Said narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, who said: Abdullah was asked about a man who divorced his wife ninety-nine times. He said: 'Three suffice you, and the rest is transgression.'"
"2271","Said narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, that al-Ala ibn Jawwanah divorced his wife a hundred divorces, so Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, sent to him: 'Withdraw from your wife.' [Flag: name uncertain in print; collation note stripped]"
"2272","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, from Ata ibn Yasar, that he was asked about a man who divorced his wife thrice before consummating with her. He said: 'Three and one are the same for a virgin.' Abdullah ibn Amr said to him: 'You are but a storyteller, not a mufti; one separates her, and three forbid her until she marries another husband.'"
"2273","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from a man who narrated to him, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, the same as that."
"2274","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Husayn and Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, who said: 'She is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.'"
"2275","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Juwaybir informed us, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas and Ibn Masud, who said: 'She is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.'"
"2276","Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: Ibn Umar divorced a wife of his, and she said to him: 'Did you see anything in me you dislike?' He said: no. She said: then for what is a chaste Muslim woman divorced? So he took her back."
"2277","Chapter on the divorce of the drunkard, and who did not recognize it and who validated it. Said narrated to us, Hazm ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Hasan, when a man asked him: 'O Abu Said, a man divorced his wife last night thrice while drinking?' He said: 'He is lashed eighty, and she is separated from him.'"
"2278","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, that they both validated the divorce of the drunkard and held that the hadd be applied."
"2279","Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, who said: 'The divorce of the drunkard is valid.'"
"2280","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, who said: 'The divorce of the drunkard is valid, and the hadd is applied, because he is in transgression.'"
"2281","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Shabi, that he used to validate the divorce of the drunkard, and whatever hadd he incurred in his drunkenness is applied to him."
"2282","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, that he used to say that also."
"2283","Said narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, who said: Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam, who said: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar saying: 'A man of the family of Abu al-Bakhtari divorced his wife while drunk, so Umar applied the hadd to him and enforced his divorce against him.'"
"2284","Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah informed me, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that he used to consider the divorce of the drunkard valid."
"2285","Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, who said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed me, from al-Hasan, the same."
"2286","Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, who said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ata, that he used to validate the divorce of one exhilarated (nashwan)."
"2287","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz: he was brought a man who divorced his wife while drunk, so he made him swear by Allah, besides whom there is no god, that he divorced without understanding; he swore, so he returned his wife to him and applied the hadd to him."
"2288","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Yahya ibn Said informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that he said as Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said."
"2289","Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, who said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Aban ibn Uthman, from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: 'Every divorce is valid except the divorce of one exhilarated (nashwan) and the divorce of the insane.'"
"2290","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: al-Amash informed us, from Ibrahim, from Abis ibn Rabiah al-Nakhai, who said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: 'Every divorce is valid except the divorce of the feeble-minded (matuh).'"
"2291","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Ashath ibn Sawwar informed us, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis informed us, from his father, that he heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying that also."
"2292","Said narrated to us, Sufyan and Abu Awanah and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abis ibn Rabiah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: 'Every divorce is valid except the divorce of the feeble-minded (matuh).'"
"2293","Said narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abis ibn Rabiah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: 'Whoever divorces, his divorce is valid, except the divorce of the feeble-minded (matuh).'"
"2294","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Ismail ibn Salim informed us, who said: I heard al-Hakam ibn Utaybah saying: 'Whoever divorces in an intoxication from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, his divorce is nothing; but whoever divorces in an intoxication from Satan, his divorce binds him.'"
"2295","Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, who said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Hakam, who said: 'He used to say about the divorce of the delirious (mubarsam), and the feverish who raves, and the marriage of the jinn, that their divorce is nothing, and that the marriage of the jinn is nothing.'"
"2296","Said narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, who said: 'The divorce of the drunkard is valid, and (that of) the delirious (mubarsam) is not valid.'"
"2297","Said narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muslim and Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, who said: 'The divorce of the insane is not valid when he divorces in his insanity; but when he regains reason, his divorce is valid.'"
"2298","Said narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muslim, from al-Shabi, who said: 'The divorce of the feeble-minded (matuh) is not valid.'"
"2299","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, and more than one of our companions, from al-Shabi - they said: 'The divorce of the insane in his lucidity is valid, but when he divorces outside his lucidity, his divorce is not valid.'"
"2300","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: 'The divorce of the insane is not valid until he recovers.'"
"2301","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Shabi, who said: 'The divorce of one overcome in his mind is not valid.'"
"2302","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, and Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Shabi, and Yunus, from al-Hasan, that they did not consider the divorce of the delirious (mubarsam) to be anything."
"2303","Said narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, who said: 'When the insane regains lucidity and reason, what he does in his lucidity is valid: manumission, divorce, hadd, or purchase.'"
"2304","Said narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydillah, from al-Shabi, who said: 'The marriage of the drunkard is not valid, but his divorce is valid.'"
"2305","Chapter on the divorce of the coerced. Said narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Qudamah ibn Ibrahim al-Jumahi narrated to us, who said: I heard my father, Qudamah ibn Ibrahim: a man in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, let himself down with a honey rope; his wife came and sat on the rope and said: 'You shall divorce her thrice, or I cut the rope.' He reminded her of Allah and Islam not to do it, but she refused: either she cuts the rope or he divorces her. So he divorced her thrice, then went to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and mentioned that to him. He said: 'Return to your family; this is not divorce.' [Flag: opening scene wording obscure in source]"
"2306","Said narrated to us, Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, who said: Umar ibn Sharahil al-Maafiri narrated to me, who said: a wife who hated her husband wanted him to divorce her but he refused; one night when she saw him sleeping, she got up, took his sword, put it on his belly, then nudged him with her foot. He said: woe to you, what is wrong with you? She said: by Allah, you shall divorce me, or I run you through with it. So he divorced her thrice. That was raised to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him; he sent to her and reviled her, saying: what drove you to what you did? She said: my hatred of him. So he enforced her divorce."
"2307","Said narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, who said: al-Ghaz ibn Jabalah al-Jublani narrated to me, from Safwan ibn Imran al-Tai: a man was sleeping with his wife; she got up, took a knife, sat on his chest, put the knife on his throat and said: 'You shall divorce me thrice outright, or I slaughter you.' He adjured her by Allah, but she refused him; so he divorced her thrice. That was mentioned to Rasul Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'There is no qailulah (heedlessness counts) in divorce.' [Flag: the word qailulah obscure here]"
"2308","Said narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Ghaz ibn Jabalah al-Jublani, that he heard Safwan al-Asamm saying: while a man was sleeping, nothing startled him but his wife sitting on his chest, placing the knife on his heart, saying: 'You shall divorce me, or I kill you.' So he divorced her, then came to Rasul Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: 'There is no qailulah in divorce; there is no qailulah in divorce.' [Flag: the word qailulah obscure here]"
"2309","Said narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, who said: I was present with Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz when a man among Banu Hatmah called al-Qummari was brought to him; some people had beaten him to divorce his wife, saying: 'By Allah, we will not leave you until we kill you or you divorce her outright.' And he brought proof of that; so he returned her to him (ruled the divorce void)."
"2310","Said narrated to us, Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, who said: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, who said: a man married the sister of Yazid ibn Muhallab in the time of al-Hajjaj, her family unwilling; when Yazid ibn al-Muhallab governed Iraq, he sent to him saying: divorce her. He refused, so Yazid beat him, saying: by Allah, I will not lift the lashes from you until you divorce her. So he divorced her. In the time of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz he came and sought his help. Umar said: 'As for his beating you, he will meet Allah with it on the Day of Resurrection; as for the divorce, it has passed (it counts).'"
"2311","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Mughirah and al-Amash informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to consider the divorce of the coerced valid. Al-Amash said: Ibrahim said: 'It is but something with which he ransomed himself.'"
"2312","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Sayyar informed us, from al-Shabi, who said: it was said to him: they claim you consider the divorce of the coerced nothing. He said: 'You lie about me while I am alive; how will you not lie about Ibrahim when he is dead?'"
"2313","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Husayn informed us, from al-Shabi, that he used to validate the divorce of the ruler under coercion, but not validate the divorce (under coercion) of robbers."
"2314","Said narrated to us, Sufyan and Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Husayn, from al-Shabi, who said: 'If robbers coerce him and he divorces, it is not valid; but if the ruler coerces him and he divorces, it is valid.'"
"2315","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Yunus and Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, that he did not consider the divorce of the coerced to be anything."
"2316","Said narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, that he did not consider the divorce of the coerced to be anything."
"2317","Said narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that he was wary of the divorce of one coerced."
"2318","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Malik and Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, that he did not consider the divorce of the coerced to be anything."
"2319","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, who said: 'Associating partners with Allah (under coercion) is greater than divorce.'"
"2320","Said narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Abdullah ibn Talhah al-Khuzai informed us, who said: Abu Yazid al-Madani narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: 'The coerced and the oppressed have no divorce.'"
"2321","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur and 'Awf informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: 'Allah Almighty has overlooked for this ummah forgetfulness, mistakes, and what they were coerced into.'"
"2322","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Allah Almighty has pardoned for you three things: mistakes, forgetfulness, and what you were coerced into.'"
"2323","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Hayyan al-'Utaridi narrated to me, from al-Hasan, he said: I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Allah Almighty has overlooked for the son of Adam what he erred in, what he forgot, what he was coerced into, and what he was overpowered by.'"
"2324","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: 'The divorce imposed by the ruler and by robbers is valid.'"
"2325","Chapter: a man swears that if he does not beat his slave one hundred lashes his wife is divorced. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, regarding a man who said to his wife: 'If I do not come to Basra then you are divorced,' he said: 'She is his wife until he dies; then if one of them dies, there is no inheritance between them.'"
"2326","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that he used to say: 'He should not approach her until he does what he swore to do.'"
"2327","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that he said regarding a man who said: 'If I do not beat my slave one hundred lashes then my wife is divorced,' he said: 'She is his wife until he beats the slave or dies.'"
"2328","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muslim, from al-Sha'bi, regarding a man who said to his slave: 'If I do not beat you then my wife is divorced,' and the slave ran away, he said: 'She is his wife until the slave dies.' Sa'id said: 'Evil is what he said.' Next chapter: 'Your rope is upon your withers,' and similar allusive expressions."
"2329","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah, that a man said to his wife: 'Your rope is upon your withers,' saying that repeatedly, then he came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, who made him swear between the Corner and the Maqam: 'What did you intend by your words?' He said: 'I intended divorce,' so he separated the two of them."
"2330","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur, Ibn Abi Layla and 'Abd al-Malik informed us, from 'Ata, that a man said to his wife: 'Your rope is upon your withers,' then he came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and mentioned that to him. Hushaym said: 'Abd al-Malik among the people said: So he sent to 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: 'Meet me in the pilgrimage season,' and he met him there, then he stood him between the Corner and the Maqam, then made him swear what he had intended by his words. He said: 'Indeed she is my cousin and the dearest of people to me, and had you stood me in any station other than this one I might have said otherwise; but since you have stood me in this station, I only intended separation from her.' So he separated the two of them."
"2331","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, regarding a man who said to his wife: 'Go, I have no need of you,' he said: 'It is three (divorces).'"
"2332","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he was asked about a man who said to his wife: 'Go and marry,' he said: 'It is nothing if he did not intend divorce.' We mentioned that to al-Sha'bi and he said: 'By Him by Whom oaths are sworn, even something lighter than this counts as divorce.'"
"2333","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, regarding a man who said to his wife: 'I have permitted you, so marry whomever you wish,' he said: 'It is nothing.' Mughirah said: So I asked al-Sha'bi about that and he said: 'Even something lighter than this counts as divorce.'"
"2334","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, regarding a man who said to his wife: 'I have permitted you to marry,' he said: 'If he meant divorce then it is divorce, otherwise it is nothing.'"
"2335","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, that they both said regarding a man who said to his wife: 'Join your family, and I have no authority over you, and the road is wide open for you,' they said: 'If he intended divorce then it is one (divorce) and he has more right to her, and if he did not intend divorce then it is nothing.'"
"2336","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about a man who said to his wife: 'You are not a wife to me,' saying that repeatedly, he said: 'I do not see it reaching three except that he intends divorce by it.'"
"2337","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, regarding a man who said to his wife: 'You are not a wife to me,' repeating that, he said: 'I do not see him saying that three times except that he intends divorce.'"
"2338","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughirah from Ibrahim, and Sayyar from al-Sha'bi, that they said regarding a man who was asked: 'Do you have a wife?' and said: 'No,' while he had a wife, they said: 'It is a lie.'"
"2339","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: He was asked about a man who was told: 'Do you have a wife?' while he had a wife, and he said: 'No,' he said: 'It is nothing; a lie he told.'"
"2340","Sa'id narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, regarding a man to whom it is said: 'Did you marry?' and he says: 'No,' and it is said: 'Do you have a wife?' and he says: 'No,' he said: 'It is nothing; a lie he told.'"
"2341","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: It used to be said: 'Divorce is what divorce was intended by.'"
"2342","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that it used to be said: 'Divorce is only what divorce was intended by.'"
"2343","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: 'Whatever divorce was intended by, it is divorce.'"
"2344","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Raja, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, he said: 'Every speech that resembles divorce, if divorce was intended by it, then it is divorce.'"
"2345","Chapter: a man has four wives and says: 'Among you is one divorce.' Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, regarding a man with four wives who said: 'Among you is one divorce,' he said: 'He divorces each one of them once.'"
"2346","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, regarding a man who said to four wives: 'I have divided one divorce among you,' he said: 'He divorces each one once, up to four divorces; then if he said five divorces, each one is divorced twice, up to eight divorces; then if he said nine divorces, each one is divorced three times.'"
"2347","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, regarding a man with four wives who said: 'My wife is divorced,' without knowing which of them he divorced, he said: 'Let him specify by intention; then if he had no intention, let him keep away from all of them.'"
"2348","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from 'Amr ibn Harim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding a man with three wives who divorced one of them once, while his intention did not fall upon any one of them, he said: 'There befalls them of divorce what befalls them of inheritance.'"
"2349","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr informed us, from 'Amr ibn Harim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, the like of it."
"2350","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: One of our companions informed me that a man from the people of Oman asked Ibn 'Abbas for a ruling, while he had wives and had divorced one of them, and Ibn 'Abbas said: 'If you had intended her in yourself and then forgot her, then they have all gone; they share in the divorce just as they share in the inheritance. And if you had not intended them, then whichever of them you wish.'"
"2351","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, and Mughirah from Ibrahim, that they both said regarding a man who divorced his wife once, then a man met him and said: 'Did you divorce your wife?' He said: 'Yes.' Then another met him and said the like of that, then another met him and said the like of his first statement, they said: 'It is his intention; if he intended his first statement then it is only one divorce.'"
"2352","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from al-Harith al-'Ukli, regarding a man who said to his four wives: 'Among you are three divorces,' he said: 'Each one is separated with three; and when he says to his wife: ""You are divorced a quarter, or a third, or a half,"" then it is a complete divorce.'"
"2353","Chapter: a man has four wives and forbids one of them from going out, then finds one of his wives has gone out and says: 'So-and-so, you are divorced' - which of them is divorced? Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, regarding a man with two wives who forbade one of them from going out, then the one who was not forbidden went out, and he thought she was the one he had forbidden, so he said: 'So-and-so, did you go out? You are divorced,' he said: 'The one he intended is divorced.' Hushaym said: And this is the position."
"2354","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: 'Both are divorced: the one in the house by his naming her, and the one who went out by his saying: ""You are divorced.""'"
"2355","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about a man with four wives, then one of them appeared and he said: 'Are you divorced?' He said: 'This is a captious puzzle.'"
"2356","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Sa'd, from al-Sunabihi, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whom he named, he said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade captious puzzles.' al-Awza'i said: Meaning wicked questions. Sa'id said: This is from Mu'awiyah, but he did not name him."
"2357","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shubrumah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: 'Intention in divorce counts in what is hidden; as for what is manifest, there is no intention in it.'"
"2358","Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ubaydillah, that al-Sha'bi said: 'When he utters divorce and intends something by it, then it is what he intended.'"
"2359","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Alqamah al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn 'Abdillah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to me, he said: 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: 'Divorce is not upon what you concealed; rather divorce is upon what came out of your mouth.'"
"2360","Chapter: a man writes the divorce of his wife. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, regarding a man who wrote the divorce of his wife and then erased it before speaking, he said: 'It is nothing unless he carries it through or speaks it.'"
"2361","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from al-Hasan, the like of that."
"2362","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he used to say: 'When he writes it, it binds him, whether he speaks it or does not speak it.'"
"2363","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: 'When a man pens divorce with his hand, it is divorce.'"
"2364","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ubaydillah, from al-Sha'bi and al-Hakam, they said: 'Whoever pens divorce with his hand, it is as he wrote.'"
"2365","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about a man who wrote to his wife while absent: 'When this letter of mine reaches you, then observe your waiting period,' but the letter did not reach her, and he died before it reached her, he said: 'It is nothing.'"
"2366","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ubaydillah, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about a man who wrote to his wife while absent: 'Observe your waiting period,' then she died before the letter reached her, he said: 'If her waiting period had not ended, he inherits her; and if her waiting period had ended, they do not inherit from one another.'"
"2367","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ubaydillah, from al-Sha'bi, that he was asked about a man who wrote to his wife: 'Observe your waiting period,' and she claimed the letter did not reach her, he said: 'As for her husband, he has uttered her divorce; it does not harm her whether his letter reached her or not, so let her do what her husband ordered her.'"
"2368","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: It was narrated to me from Tawus, that he said regarding a man who said to his wife: 'Prosper!' he said: 'If he intended her divorce by it, then it is divorce.'"
"2369","Chapter: a man's wife says to him: 'Describe me.' Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he was asked about a man whose wife said to him: 'Describe me,' and he said: 'You are like a gazelle, you are like a dove.' She said: 'I will not be satisfied until you say: freed and divorced.' So he said that, while meaning she-camels freed from their hobbles. Ibrahim said: 'She is divorced.' Mughirah said: 'Why? Was it not said: divorce is what divorce was intended by?' Ibrahim said to me: 'Do you not see that he says to her face: ""You are freed and divorced""?'"
"2370","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, the like of it, but he did not say: dove."
"2371","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Hakam, from Khaythamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Abdullah ibn Shihab al-Khawlani, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought such a case, and he said to her husband: 'Give her head a beating, and if he divorces by it then she is your wife.' Hushaym said: And this is the position."
"2372","Chapter: a man dies leaving his wife in a foreign land. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah, he said: 'When a man dies leaving his wife while absent, or divorces while absent, then the waiting period falls upon her from the day he dies or divorces her.'"
"2373","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that he said the like of that."
"2374","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Mujahid and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: 'She observes her waiting period from the day he died or divorced.'"
"2375","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: 'She observes her waiting period from the day he died.'"
"2376","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, he said: I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr, Mujahid, 'Ata, Abu Qilabah, Muhammad ibn Sirin and 'Ikrimah, and they said: 'From the day he died.' He said: And Jabir ibn Zayd and Ibn 'Abbas said: 'From the day he died.'"
"2377","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: 'The waiting period is from the day he died or divorced.'"
"2378","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah and al-Shaybani informed me, from al-Sha'bi, he said the like of that."
"2379","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, regarding a man who divorced his wife at each menstruation, he said: 'Her waiting period is from the first divorce, so long as there was no retraction.'"
"2380","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah and 'Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, and Muhammad ibn Salim from al-Sha'bi, they said the like of that."
"2381","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, he said: 'She observes her waiting period from the first divorce.'"
"2382","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, the like of the statement of al-Hasan and Abu Qilabah."
"2383","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn 'Ubayd informed us, from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah, he said: 'She observes her waiting period from the first divorce, if he took her back, so long as he did not consummate with her.'"
"2384","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath and Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, that Ibn Mas'ud said: 'The waiting period is from the day he died or divorced.'"
"2385","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Husayn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, he said: 'The waiting period is from the day he died or divorced.'"
"2386","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, the like of that."
"2387","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath informed us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabi'ah ibn Najid, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: 'The waiting period is from the day the news reaches her.'"
"2388","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, he said: 'If evidence is established then from the day he died or divorced, and if no evidence is established then from the day the news reaches her.'"
"2389","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, Abu al-'Aliyah and Ibn Sirin, that they said: 'From the day he died or the day he divorced.'"
"2390","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: 'The waiting period is from the day he died or the day he divorced.'"
"2391","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, regarding a man who divorced his wife once, then travelled, then wrote to her of another divorce, he said: 'Inheritance is between them so long as she has not bathed after the third menstruation from the day he divorced her; except that when the news reaches her after that, she observes her waiting period from the day the news reaches her, and there is no inheritance between them in the latter waiting period.'"
"2392","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus and Mansur informed me, from al-Hasan, he said: 'The waiting period is from the day the news reaches her; then if he divorced her once or twice, up to her becoming pure after the third menstruation, except that she observes her waiting period from the day the news reaches her, and there is no inheritance between them in the latter waiting period.' Hushaym said: The position is what 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said."
"2393","Chapter: a man divorces his wife, she menstruates three times, then he comes in to her before she becomes pure. Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, that a man of the Ansar divorced his wife, then she menstruated three times; and when she went in to bathe, he wanted to go in to her but was prevented from that, and she was a modest woman, so they disputed to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab. She said: 'I saw purity, removed my clothes, and brought the water near.' He said: 'Had you checked yourself with a cloth?' She said: 'No.' So he returned her to him."
"2394","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from 'Umar, the like of that."
"2395","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Umar and 'Abdullah, they said: 'He has more right to her so long as she has not bathed after the third menstruation.'"
"2396","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, the like of it."
"2397","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, the like of that."
"2398","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from Makhul, that Abu al-Darda and 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit said the like of that."
"2399","Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, the like of it."
"2400","Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Ubaydillah ibn 'Ubayd al-Kala'i, from Makhul, that Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, 'Ali, Ibn Mas'ud, Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, Abu al-Darda and 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: 'He has more right to take her back so long as she has not bathed after the third menstruation.'"
